3.0},{\"vid\":\"AdKNCBrkZQ4\",\"title\":\"Low Latency Routing in Space\",\"channel\":\"HotNets Anonymous\",\"summary\":\"A short visualization from HotNets researchers of routing and latency over SpaceX's proposed Starlink constellation, based on its FCC filings. It shows orbital shells, link topology and how inter-satellite routes could beat terrestrial fiber on long distances.\",\"why_hn\":\"It is the go-to visual for how Starlink's constellation and laser links could cut global latency, linked in many satellite internet threads.\",\"content_type\":\"demo\",\"level\":\"intermediate\",\"primary_topic\":\"satellite network routing\",\"categories\":[\"Networking & internet infrastructure\",\"Space exploration & spaceflight\"],\"tags\":[\"starlink\",\"leo constellation\",\"latency\",\"routing simulation\",\"spacex\"],\"quote\":\"This video goes a bit into the probable topology of the links and gives a good look at how the eventual constellation would look.\",\"recommenders\":4,\"score\":3.0},{\"vid\":\"AdKUJxjn-R8\",\"title\":\"Forget big change, start with a tiny habit: BJ Fogg at TEDxFremont\",\"channel\":\"TEDx Talks\",\"summary\":\"BJ Fogg of Stanford's Persuasive Tech Lab argues that lasting change comes from tiny habits, such as flossing one tooth or doing one pushup, anchored to things you already do.\",\"why_hn\":\"Recommended in habit and motivation threads for its simple anchor-then-tiny-action recipe.\",\"content_type\":\"talk\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"habit formation\",\"categories\":[\"Productivity & self-improvement\",\"Psychology & human behavior\"],\"tags\":[\"tiny habits\",\"bj fogg\",\"behavior change\",\"motivation\",\"tedx\"],\"quote\":\"After I X, I will do Y. X must be sure, Y must be small.\",\"recommenders\":3,\"score\":3.0},{\"vid\":\"Ag1AKIl_2GM\",\"title\":\"Free software, free society: Richard Stallman at TEDxGeneva 2014\",\"channel\":\"TEDx Talks\",\"summary\":\"Richard Stallman's TEDxGeneva 2014 talk describing how nonfree programs give companies control over users and what users can do to regain control. It introduces the free software movement and the four freedoms.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN uses it constantly as the reference for the argument that either the user controls the software or the software controls the user, and it is recommended as a basic introduction.\",\"content_type\":\"talk\",\"level\":\"intro\",\"primary_topic\":\"free software philosophy\",\"categories\":[\"Hacker culture & free software\",\"Linux & open-source ecosystems\"],\"tags\":[\"richard stallman\",\"free software\",\"user freedom\",\"gnu\",\"software control\"],\"quote\":\"I'd recommend this[1] talk by Richard Stallman, it's pretty basic, but it gets the idea across well.\",\"recommenders\":2,\"score\":3.0},{\"vid\":\"AnaASTBn_K4\",\"title\":\"How does a whip break the sound barrier? (Slow Motion Shockwave formation) - Smarter Every Day 207\",\"channel\":\"SmarterEveryDay\",\"summary\":\"Smarter Every Day uses high-speed and Schlieren photography to show how a whip crack is a supersonic shockwave formed at the tip. It references academic papers on whip physics.\",\"why_hn\":\"Recommended as the clearest footage of a whip tip going supersonic, and cited in shockwave discussions.\",\"content_type\":\"explainer\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"whip crack shockwaves\",\"categories\":[\"Everyday physics & science demos\",\"Fundamental physics\"],\"tags\":[\"schlieren photography\",\"supersonic\",\"shockwave\",\"slow motion\",\"physics\"],\"quote\":\"I highly recommend it.\",\"recommenders\":2,\"score\":3.0},{\"vid\":\"Ao9iOeK_jvU\",\"title\":\"Chess Fundamentals #1: Undefended Pieces\",\"channel\":\"John Bartholomew\",\"summary\":\"First video in John Bartholomew's Chess Fundamentals series, focused on spotting undefended pieces. He teaches habits for scanning your own and your opponent's position to avoid hanging pieces.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN chess improvers recommend Bartholomew's beginner playlist as a clear, approachable path to getting better.\",\"content_type\":\"lecture\",\"level\":\"intro\",\"primary_topic\":\"chess fundamentals\",\"categories\":[\"Chess, board games & puzzles\"],\"tags\":[\"chess\",\"tactics\",\"beginner chess\",\"blunder prevention\",\"undefended pieces\"],\"quote\":\"I'd recommend these youtube videos [1] by John Bartholomew.\",\"recommenders\":3,\"score\":3.0},{\"vid\":\"AwX9G38vdCE\",\"title\":\"The Boring Company Information Session\",\"channel\":\"The Boring Company\",\"summary\":\"A long information session where The Boring Company presents its vision for Loop, an underground high-speed transit system, and the traffic problems it aims to solve. It includes discussion of faster tunnel boring and electrification.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN commenters point to it as the primary source for what the company is actually proposing, in threads skeptical of the project.\",\"content_type\":\"talk\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"underground tunnel transit\",\"categories\":[\"Transit, cities & urban planning\",\"Civil engineering & construction\",\"Tech industry & business models\"],\"tags\":[\"boring company\",\"tunneling\",\"loop\",\"urban transportation\",\"elon musk\"],\"quote\":\"It's worth watching to see what they are proposing.\",\"recommenders\":3,\"score\":3.0},{\"vid\":\"AxJubaijQbI\",\"title\":\"The Best (and Worst) Ways to Shuffle Cards - Numberphile\",\"channel\":\"Numberphile\",\"summary\":\"Persi Diaconis explains on Numberphile the mathematics of card shuffling, including why seven riffle shuffles are needed to randomize a deck and how different shuffles compare.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN points to it as a good, anecdote-filled introduction to the math of shuffling from the expert himself.\",\"content_type\":\"interview\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"mathematics of card shuffling\",\"categories\":[\"Probability & game theory\",\"Recreational & visual math\"],\"tags\":[\"persi diaconis\",\"shuffling\",\"randomness\",\"probability\",\"numberphile\"],\"quote\":\"It gives a lot of insight and anectdotes in addition to the central theorem\",\"recommenders\":3,\"score\":3.0},{\"vid\":\"AyORieDhpkg\",\"title\":\"The Kilimanjaro Darkjazz Ensemble - Here Be Dragons (Full Album)\",\"channel\":\"Ivica Stojkov\",\"summary\":\"A full-length album by The Kilimanjaro Darkjazz Ensemble, a dark, cinematic electronic jazz group. It runs about 55 minutes across nine tracks.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN commenters suggest it as atmospheric, near-ambient music for programming and focus.\",\"content_type\":\"music\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"dark electronic jazz\",\"categories\":[\"Music performance & songs\"],\"tags\":[\"darkjazz\",\"ambient\",\"electronic jazz\",\"focus music\",\"full album\"],\"quote\":\"still in the spirit of heavy, nearly ambient\",\"recommenders\":3,\"score\":3.0},{\"vid\":\"BCiZc0n6COY\",\"title\":\"Lecture 1: Introduction to Information Theory\",\"channel\":\"Jakob Foerster\",\"summary\":\"The first lecture of David MacKay's Cambridge course on information theory, pattern recognition and neural networks. It introduces the core ideas of his book Information Theory, Inference, and Learning Algorithms.\",\"why_hn\":\"Recommended as an enjoyable, clear introduction to information theory that pairs well with MacKay's free textbook.\",\"content_type\":\"lecture\",\"level\":\"intro\",\"primary_topic\":\"information theory\",\"categories\":[\"Information theory & signal processing\",\"University lectures & courses\",\"Machine learning & deep learning\"],\"tags\":[\"david mackay\",\"information theory\",\"inference\",\"machine learning\",\"cambridge\"],\"quote\":\"It was very enjoyable for me to learn the material from his lectures.\",\"recommenders\":3,\"score\":3.0},{\"vid\":\"BKP1I7IocYU\",\"title\":\"Why It's Rude to Suck at Warcraft\",\"channel\":\"Folding Ideas\",\"summary\":\"Folding Ideas' long essay on why playing poorly in World of Warcraft feels rude. It traces how raiding culture shifted from relaxed fun to optimization, theorycrafting and wikis.\",\"why_hn\":\"Recommended as a thoughtful, research-heavy dive into game culture and the social pressure of competitive play.\",\"content_type\":\"documentary\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"world of warcraft culture\",\"categories\":[\"Gaming culture & analysis\"],\"tags\":[\"wow\",\"raiding\",\"theorycrafting\",\"game culture\",\"folding ideas\"],\"quote\":\"is worth the watch\",\"recommenders\":3,\"score\":3.0},{\"vid\":\"BTHvs3V8DBA\",\"title\":\"High Performance Web Sites and YSlow\",\"channel\":\"Google TechTalks\",\"summary\":\"A Google Tech Talk on Yahoo's 14 rules for faster web pages and the YSlow tool. It covers front-end practices like avoiding @import and fixing ETags, with live analysis of popular sites.\",\"why_hn\":\"Praised as solid, research-backed advice on front-end web performance.\",\"content_type\":\"talk\",\"level\":\"intermediate\",\"primary_topic\":\"web performance\",\"categories\":[\"Web development\",\"Software performance & optimization\"],\"tags\":[\"yslow\",\"front-end performance\",\"caching\",\"page load\",\"yahoo\"],\"quote\":\"Everything they produce about the subject (and I don't just mean the plugin) is solid gold.\",\"recommenders\":2,\"score\":3.0},{\"vid\":\"BTlUyS-T-_4\",\"title\":\"The REAL reason behind the housing crisis\",\"channel\":\"Garys Economics\",\"summary\":\"Gary's Economics argues that the UK housing crisis stems from wealth inequality, treating housing as an asset like shares that rich people bid up. He contends that simply building more housing won't fix affordability.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN commenters share it as a counterargument to the YIMBY build-more-housing view, linking wealth concentration to asset prices.\",\"content_type\":\"commentary\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"housing economics\",\"categories\":[\"Labor, work & inequality\",\"Microeconomics & behavioral economics\"],\"tags\":[\"housing crisis\",\"wealth inequality\",\"house prices\",\"yimby debate\",\"uk economy\"],\"quote\":\"It feels to me like a good faith counterargument to the YIMBY build more housing line of thought, so might be an interesting perspective\",\"recommenders\":3,\"score\":3.0},{\"vid\":\"BXmOlCy0oBM\",\"title\":\"Erlang: The Movie (Fixed Audio)\",\"channel\":\"CH1LLW4VE\",\"summary\":\"A 12-minute film in which Erlang's creators demonstrate the language's fault tolerance and live-system features, including phoning each other to show it working. This version has fixed audio.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN recommends it as a charming, concise demonstration of what makes Erlang special, from the people who built it.\",\"content_type\":\"demo\",\"level\":\"intro\",\"primary_topic\":\"erlang fault tolerance\",\"categories\":[\"Functional programming\",\"Distributed systems\",\"History of computing\"],\"tags\":[\"erlang\",\"fault tolerance\",\"concurrency\",\"telecom\",\"programming languages\"],\"quote\":\"the most glorious 11 minutes of some programmers explaining how their creation works you will ever see\",\"recommenders\":2,\"score\":3.0},{\"vid\":\"Bca5_uyH9E4\",\"title\":\"Meeting my hero! Sailing legend Sven Yrvind\",\"channel\":\"Sam Holmes Sailing\",\"summary\":\"Sam Holmes Sailing visits sailing legend Sven Yrvind and tours his boat, covering the man and his small-boat design philosophy.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN recommends it as an accessible introduction to Yrvind and his minimalist boat ideas.\",\"content_type\":\"interview\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"small boat sailing\",\"categories\":[\"Ships, submarines & maritime\",\"Product & industrial design\"],\"tags\":[\"sven yrvind\",\"sailing\",\"boat design\",\"minimalism\",\"vlog\"],\"quote\":\"I watched this video [1] to get an idea about the man and his boat design philosophy and it's very cool.\",\"recommenders\":3,\"score\":3.0},{\"vid\":\"Bd2bbHoVQSM\",\"title\":\"Timeshares: Last Week Tonight with John Oliver (HBO)\",\"channel\":\"Las