er writing\"],\"quote\":\"thanks to them I have learned a lot about movies, actors, directors and movie making in general.\",\"recommenders\":2,\"score\":3.0},{\"vid\":\"G1m0aX9Lpts\",\"title\":\"Sam Aaron live coding an ambient electro set w/ Sonic Pi\",\"channel\":\"Sam Aaron\",\"summary\":\"Sam Aaron live codes an ambient electronic set using Sonic Pi, the music programming environment he created. The performance shows code driving music in real time.\",\"why_hn\":\"Offered as an example of live-coded music and a fun entry point to Sonic Pi.\",\"content_type\":\"demo\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"live coding music\",\"categories\":[\"Creative coding & generative art\",\"Music theory, synthesis & production\",\"Music performance & songs\"],\"tags\":[\"sonic pi\",\"live coding\",\"ambient music\",\"electronic music\",\"algorave\"],\"quote\":\"Sam Aaron is the guy behind the project, he does a lot of ambient type stuff\",\"recommenders\":3,\"score\":3.0},{\"vid\":\"G4hL5Om4IJ4\",\"title\":\"Jim Keller: The Future of Computing, AI, Life, and Consciousness | Lex Fridman Podcast #162\",\"channel\":\"Lex Fridman\",\"summary\":\"Lex Fridman interviews chip architect Jim Keller about the future of computing, AI, life and consciousness. Topics include CPU design, branch prediction and why imperfect designs often win.\",\"why_hn\":\"Recommended as a stellar long-form interview with someone both very smart and wise, mined for CPU design insights.\",\"content_type\":\"interview\",\"level\":\"intermediate\",\"primary_topic\":\"computer architecture\",\"categories\":[\"Computer architecture & CPUs\",\"Tech pioneers & interviews\",\"AI safety, AGI & impact\"],\"tags\":[\"jim keller\",\"cpu design\",\"branch prediction\",\"lex fridman\",\"ai hardware\"],\"quote\":\"Investing time to listen to the guy seems to be not worse.\",\"recommenders\":3,\"score\":3.0},{\"vid\":\"GC-0tCy4P1U\",\"title\":\"Twitter and Visual Studio Rant\",\"channel\":\"Molly Rocket\",\"summary\":\"Casey Muratori responds on-stream to a dismissive Twitter post by demonstrating how slow Visual Studio's startup and debugger watch window are, comparing it to much older software and machines. It is a long rant about software performance and bloat.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN commenters cite it as the canonical concrete demonstration that modern developer tools got slower despite vastly faster hardware.\",\"content_type\":\"commentary\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"software performance\",\"categories\":[\"Software performance & optimization\",\"Testing, debugging & developer tools\"],\"tags\":[\"visual studio\",\"debugger\",\"software bloat\",\"performance\",\"casey muratori\"],\"quote\":\"Casey Muratori has some great YouTube videos (a.k.a.: rants)\",\"recommenders\":3,\"score\":3.0},{\"vid\":\"Gh-Tff7DdzU\",\"title\":\"RAAIS 2017 - Simon Knowles, Co-Founder and CTO of Graphcore\",\"channel\":\"The Research and Applied AI Summit - RAAIS\",\"summary\":\"Simon Knowles, co-founder and CTO of Graphcore, talks about \\\"intelligence processors\\\", chips designed specifically for machine learning. The talk was given at the RAAIS 2017 summit and covers Graphcore's architecture.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN points to it as a technical talk from a chip designer on why AI hardware should put memory close to compute and use async data transfers.\",\"content_type\":\"talk\",\"level\":\"advanced\",\"primary_topic\":\"ai accelerator chips\",\"categories\":[\"Computer architecture & CPUs\",\"Machine learning & deep learning\"],\"tags\":[\"graphcore\",\"ai hardware\",\"deep learning\",\"processor architecture\",\"memory bandwidth\"],\"quote\":\"Here's a nice technical talk from Graphcore's CTO about that\",\"recommenders\":3,\"score\":3.0},{\"vid\":\"Gj8IA6xOpSk\",\"title\":\"The call to learn | Clifford Stoll\",\"channel\":\"TED\",\"summary\":\"Clifford Stoll's energetic TED talk, a wandering mix of anecdotes, a science experiment and thoughts on curiosity, education and technology