tem\",\"categories\":[\"Software practice, open source & careers\",\"Startups & entrepreneurship\",\"Internet culture & memes\"],\"tags\":[\"emojli\",\"tom scott\",\"emoji\",\"app development\",\"side projects\"],\"quote\":\"There is a wonderful talk by the founders of emoj.li about how it was all a joke which got out of hand.\",\"recommenders\":3,\"score\":3.0},{\"vid\":\"Gxd23UVID7k\",\"title\":\"Leonard Cohen - Everybody Knows (Official Audio)\",\"channel\":\"LeonardCohenVEVO\",\"summary\":\"The official audio of Leonard Cohen's 'Everybody Knows' from the album I'm Your Man.\",\"why_hn\":\"Commenters name it among their favourite Cohen songs, especially in threads after his death.\",\"content_type\":\"music\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"leonard cohen songs\",\"categories\":[\"Music performance & songs\"],\"tags\":[\"leonard cohen\",\"songwriting\",\"i'm your man\",\"folk\"],\"quote\":\"I don't know what it is about that song that keeps me coming back.\",\"recommenders\":3,\"score\":3.0},{\"vid\":\"H62hZJVqs2o\",\"title\":\"\\\"Uptime 15,364 days - The Computers of Voyager\\\" by Aaron Cummings\",\"channel\":\"Strange Loop Conference\",\"summary\":\"A Strange Loop 2019 talk by Aaron Cummings on the computing systems aboard Voyager 1 and 2, which control the spacecraft and record and return data decades after launch in 1977.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN recommends it in Voyager threads as a good talk on how these old computers have proved durable and adaptable.\",\"content_type\":\"talk\",\"level\":\"intermediate\",\"primary_topic\":\"voyager spacecraft computers\",\"categories\":[\"Space exploration & spaceflight\",\"Embedded systems & DIY electronics\",\"History of computing\"],\"tags\":[\"voyager\",\"nasa\",\"spacecraft computing\",\"embedded systems\",\"legacy systems\"],\"quote\":\"this talk was really good\",\"recommenders\":3,\"score\":3.0},{\"vid\":\"HBluLfX2F_k\",\"title\":\"You've (Likely) Been Playing The Game Of Life Wrong\",\"channel\":\"Veritasium\",\"summary\":\"Veritasium explains why many real-world systems follow power laws rather than normal distributions. It covers self-organized criticality, with simulations of sandpiles, magnetism and forest fires.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN commenters recommend it for changing how they think about distributions and for showing how criticality shows up across earthquakes, wildfires and other fields.\",\"content_type\":\"explainer\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"power laws and criticality\",\"categories\":[\"Everyday physics & science demos\",\"Data science & statistics\",\"Scientific method & science communication\"],\"tags\":[\"power law\",\"self-organized criticality\",\"statistics\",\"simulations\",\"percolation\"],\"quote\":\"Before I watched this I would default to thinking about most distributions as normal.\",\"recommenders\":4,\"score\":3.0},{\"vid\":\"HNkLcD3PKyk\",\"title\":\"What It Really Takes to Convert an Office Building to Apartments | Odd Lots\",\"channel\":\"Bloomberg Podcasts\",\"summary\":\"An Odd Lots podcast episode on why converting empty office buildings into apartments is hard. A managing director at Vanbarton Group walks through the zoning, financing and construction obstacles, mostly in New York.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN links it whenever office-to-residential conversion comes up, as a good deep dive into why the idea is not simple.\",\"content_type\":\"podcast\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"office-to-residential conversion\",\"categories\":[\"Transit, cities & urban planning\",\"Civil engineering & construction\",\"Business & economics (other)\"],\"tags\":[\"real estate\",\"zoning\",\"housing\",\"office vacancy\",\"construction\"],\"quote\":\"a good deep dive into why this is not a simple proposition.\",\"recommenders\":3,\"score\":3.0},{\"vid\":\"HQKy1KJpSVc\",\"title\":\"How Does Kodak Make Film? (Kodak Factory Tour Part 1 of 3) - Smarter Every Day 271\",\"channel\":\"SmarterEveryDay\",\"summary\":\"Destin Sandlin of Smarter Every Day tours a Kodak factory to show how photographic film is manufactured. This is part one of a three-part series covering the large-scale coating and production process.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN viewers find the film manufacturing process and the engineering behind it fascinating, especially the continuous roll changes.\",\"content_type\":\"documentary\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"film manufacturing\",\"categories\":[\"Manufacturing & industrial processes\",\"Chemistry\",\"Visual arts, photography & architecture\"],\"tags\":[\"kodak\",\"photographic film\",\"factory tour\",\"manufacturing\",\"engineering\"],\"quote\":\"it’s a fascinating look at the process of film manufacturing\",\"recommenders\":3,\"score\":3.0},{\"vid\":\"HStF1RJOyxI\",\"title\":\"Making R run Fast - Jan Vitek\",\"channel\":\"John O'Neill\",\"summary\":\"Jan Vitek of Northeastern University gives a meetup talk on the challenges of making the R language run fast. He explains what in R's semantics makes it hard to optimize and to build a JIT compiler for.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN points to it as the best explanation of why R is so hard to optimize, often paired with talks on Python and used to explain what makes Julia fast.\",\"content_type\":\"talk\",\"level\":\"advanced\",\"primary_topic\":\"language implementation and optimization\",\"categories\":[\"Compilers, interpreters & program analysis\",\"Software performance & optimization\",\"Data science & statistics\"],\"tags\":[\"r language\",\"jit compilers\",\"performance\",\"language semantics\",\"fastr\"],\"quote\":\"Another talk on the difficulty of optimising R is this fantastic one by Jan Vitek\",\"recommenders\":3,\"score\":3.0},{\"vid\":\"HVv_IQKlafQ\",\"title\":\"3D Gaussian Splatting - Why Graphics Will Never Be The Same\",\"channel\":\"IndividualKex\",\"summary\":\"A two-minute explainer of 3D Gaussian Splatting, the rendering technique from a 2023 research paper. It outlines why it could change how 3D graphics are made.\",\"why_hn\":