see what Kildall was like in real life and as a tribute to an influential figure.\",\"content_type\":\"documentary\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"gary kildall and cp/m\",\"categories\":[\"History of computing\",\"Tech pioneers & interviews\"],\"tags\":[\"gary kildall\",\"cp/m\",\"computer history\",\"computer chronicles\",\"personal computers\"],\"quote\":\"If you want to know how was he IRL I recommend watching Computer chronicles.\",\"recommenders\":3,\"score\":3.0},{\"vid\":\"Tfh0ytz8S0k\",\"title\":\"How \\\"oldschool\\\" graphics worked Part 1 - Commodore and Nintendo\",\"channel\":\"The 8-Bit Guy\",\"summary\":\"The 8-Bit Guy explains the color limitations of 1980s computers and consoles such as the NES and Commodore 64. It shows how sprites, attributes and palettes shaped the look of old games.\",\"why_hn\":\"Recommended as a clear, approachable explanation of how retro graphics hardware actually worked.\",\"content_type\":\"explainer\",\"level\":\"intro\",\"primary_topic\":\"retro graphics hardware\",\"categories\":[\"Demoscene & retrocomputing\",\"Game history & retro gaming\",\"Computer architecture & CPUs\"],\"tags\":[\"nes\",\"commodore 64\",\"sprites\",\"color limitations\",\"8-bit\"],\"quote\":\"The 8-Bit Guy has some great videos about how graphics worked on the older systems\",\"recommenders\":4,\"score\":3.0},{\"vid\":\"TqKQ94DtS54\",\"title\":\"Arcologies\",\"channel\":\"Isaac Arthur\",\"summary\":\"An Isaac Arthur episode on arcologies, self-sufficient habitats that could house whole cities, on Earth or on harsh worlds. It covers how such structures might work and what limits their size.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN commenters point to it in population and megacity discussions, mainly for its estimates of how many people arcologies could support and the heat, power and elevator bottlenecks.\",\"content_type\":\"explainer\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"arcologies and megastructures\",\"categories\":[\"Futurism & technology and society\",\"Civil engineering & construction\",\"Cosmology & astrophysics\"],\"tags\":[\"arcology\",\"megacities\",\"future habitats\",\"sustainability\",\"isaac arthur\"],\"quote\":\"Isaac Arthur's YouTube channel is full of speculation and plans for all kinds of possible or nearly-possible futures\",\"recommenders\":3,\"score\":3.0},{\"vid\":\"TshYfYIxR9E\",\"title\":\"Light Waves Visualized using Photon Sieves.\",\"channel\":\"Huygens Optics\",\"summary\":\"Huygens Optics shows how DIY photon sieves shape a laser's wave front, explaining how they differ from zone plates and how aperture count affects the focal point, with time-resolved visualizations of the diffraction.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN points to it for a clear explanation of photon sieves versus Fresnel lenses and for showing what interference patterns actually look like.\",\"content_type\":\"explainer\",\"level\":\"intermediate\",\"primary_topic\":\"photon sieves and diffraction optics\",\"categories\":[\"Everyday physics & science demos\",\"Fundamental physics\"],\"tags\":[\"photon sieve\",\"diffraction\",\"fresnel zone plate\",\"optics\",\"lithography\",\"wave front\"],\"quote\":\"It shows how the interference patterns actually look.\",\"recommenders\":3,\"score\":3.0},{\"vid\":\"UE-k4hYHIDE\",\"title\":\"The Only Famous Motherboard\",\"channel\":\"Cathode Ray Dude - CRD\",\"summary\":\"Cathode Ray Dude's hour-long retrospective on the ABIT BP6, the dual-Celeron motherboard. He covers early multiprocessing, its legend, a build, running NT 4, benchmarks and the pros and cons of early SMP.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN recommends it as an excellent history of the famous ABIT BP6 board.\",\"content_type\":\"documentary\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"abit bp6 motherboard\",\"categories\":[\"Computer architecture & CPUs\",\"Demoscene & retrocomputing\"],\"tags\":[\"abit bp6\",\"dual celeron\",\"smp\",\"retro hardware\",\"windows nt 4\"],\"quote\":\"Cathode Ray Dude's channel has a great video about the history of this