65FRxE7uMc\",\"title\":\"Badness 0 (Apostrophe‛s version)\",\"channel\":\"suckerpinch\",\"summary\":\"Tom 7's pilot episode of a series that plays with type systems and absurd programming, presented as a parody of the GPL v3 license. It mixes a typesetting experiment with a long, story-driven intro on the origin of TeX. Source code and papers are linked from the author's site.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN readers point to it as an example of Tom7's ridiculous-but-brilliant programming projects, here tied to license parody and typesetting.\",\"content_type\":\"talk\",\"level\":\"intermediate\",\"primary_topic\":\"programming humor and typesetting\",\"categories\":[\"Satire & parody\",\"Programming language design\",\"Graphic design & typography\"],\"tags\":[\"tom7\",\"type systems\",\"tex\",\"gpl parody\",\"typesetting\"],\"quote\":\"this fun experiment in Typesetting which starts off with the amazing TeX origin story\",\"recommenders\":4,\"score\":3.0},{\"vid\":\"YAtLTLiqNwg\",\"title\":\"Elon Musk Interview: 1-on-1 with Sandy Munro\",\"channel\":\"Munro Live\",\"summary\":\"Sandy Munro interviews Elon Musk at Boca Chica about Tesla production, mega-castings, seats, structural battery packs and the difficulty of mass production.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN uses it as a primary source on Tesla manufacturing and engineering decisions and Musk's grasp of product detail.\",\"content_type\":\"interview\",\"level\":\"intermediate\",\"primary_topic\":\"tesla manufacturing\",\"categories\":[\"Cars, EVs & motorcycles\",\"Manufacturing & industrial processes\",\"Tech pioneers & interviews\"],\"tags\":[\"elon musk\",\"sandy munro\",\"gigacasting\",\"mass production\",\"tesla\"],\"quote\":\"Check out this video of Musk and Sandy Munro (former Chief Engineer at Ford) talking about it\",\"recommenders\":3,\"score\":3.0},{\"vid\":\"YGLNyHd2w10\",\"title\":\"I Solved Klotski\",\"channel\":\"2swap\",\"summary\":\"2swap explains how he solved the Klotski sliding-block puzzle by mapping its full state space as a graph and visualizing it. The video includes footage of the Guinness world-record solve and links to an interactive graph.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN people point to it for intuition about why some games are hard to navigate and for its Rush Hour and graph visualizations.\",\"content_type\":\"explainer\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"puzzle state spaces\",\"categories\":[\"Chess, board games & puzzles\",\"Algorithms & data structures\",\"Data visualization & information design\"],\"tags\":[\"klotski\",\"rush hour\",\"graph visualization\",\"puzzle solving\",\"state space\"],\"quote\":\"the state space of the game can produce some intuition on why certain games are hard\",\"recommenders\":3,\"score\":3.0},{\"vid\":\"YMqgiXLjvRs\",\"title\":\"Y Combinator's Paul Graham sits down with Jason at LAUNCH Festival 2014\",\"channel\":\"This Week in Startups\",\"summary\":\"A fireside chat at LAUNCH Festival 2014 where Paul Graham tells Jason Calacanis why he is handing Y Combinator's presidency to Sam Altman. He also shares startup advice drawn from nine years and 500+ startups.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN people link it for Paul Graham's candid views on startups, Aaron Swartz, and investing selection.\",\"content_type\":\"interview\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"startups and y combinator\",\"categories\":[\"Startups & entrepreneurship\",\"Tech pioneers & interviews\"],\"tags\":[\"paul graham\",\"y combinator\",\"startup advice\",\"sam altman\",\"founders\"],\"quote\":\"PG definitely gives up lots of great success tips, so worth watching it all.\",\"recommenders\":3,\"score\":3.0},{\"vid\":\"YdOXS_9_P4U\",\"title\":\"Terence Tao on the cosmic distance ladder\",\"channel\":\"3Blue1Brown\",\"summary\":\"Terence Tao and Grant Sanderson of 3Blue1Brown walk through the cosmic distance ladder, showing how humans measured distances from the Earth to the Moon, Sun, planets and beyond. It includes animations and the history behind each step.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN recommends it as an excellent explanation of how we know cosmic distances.\",\"content_type\":\"explainer\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"cosmic distance ladder\",\"categories\":[\"Cosmology & astrophysics\",\"Recreational & visual math\"],\"tags\":[\"astronomy\",\"terence tao\",\"3blue1brown\",\"distance measurement\",\"history of science\"],\"quote\":\"For details, watch the video, it is really good.\",\"recommenders\":2,\"score\":3.0},{\"vid\":\"YdiZa0Y3F3c\",\"title\":\"Shared memory parallelism in Julia | Kiran Pamnany | Cambridge Julia Meetup (May 2018)\",\"channel\":\"The Julia Programming Language\",\"summary\":\"Kiran Pamnany's Cambridge Julia Meetup talk on Julia's shared memory parallelism and its new task scheduler. It argues that fork-join and work-stealing models nest poorly and presents depth-first scheduling for composable parallelism.\",\"why_hn\":\"Recommended in Julia threading threads as an insightful, simple explanation of the new task scheduler.\",\"content_type\":\"talk\",\"level\":\"advanced\",\"primary_topic\":\"parallel task scheduling\",\"categories\":[\"Software performance & optimization\",\"Python, Ruby & scripting languages\",\"Operating systems & kernels\"],\"tags\":[\"julia\",\"multithreading\",\"task scheduler\",\"composable parallelism\",\"hpc\"],\"quote\":\"I found his talk to be an insightful overview of this work\",\"recommenders\":4,\"score\":3.0},{\"vid\":\"Z20XNp-luNA\",\"title\":\"Ichthyology: Phishing as a Science\",\"channel\":\"Black Hat\",\"summary\":\"Karla Burnett presents real phishing campaigns run against a Bay Area tech company, including conversion rates and how existing protections were bypassed. She argues for evidence-based techniques to prevent credential phishing, not just mitigate it.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN people cite it to show even technical users fall for phishing and that hardware security keys are the real fix.\",\"content_type\":\"talk\",\"level\":\"intermediate\",\"primary_topic\":\"phishing defense\",\"categories\":[\"Security & hacking\",\"Privacy, surveillance & cybercrime\"],\"tags\":[\"phishing\",\"security keys\",\"black hat\",\"credential theft\",\"social engineering\"],\"quote\":\"shows just how easy it is to phish even users who think they are too good to be fooled.\",\"recommenders\":3,\"score\":3.0},{\"vid\":\"Z8ZhQPaw4rE\",\"title\":\"Solaris | SCIENCE FICTION | FULL MOVIE | directed by Tarkovsky\",\"channel\":\"Mosfilm\",\"summary\":\"Andrei Tarkovsky's 1972 film Solaris, in which a psychologist is sent to a space station orbiting a planet with an alien intelligence and meets his dead wife there. It is the full movie, uploaded by Mosfilm.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN recommends it as a masterpiece of emotional, contemplative science fiction, and draws analogies between its alien ocean and AI.\",\"content_type\":\"other\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"tarkovsky science fiction film\",\"categories\":[\"Film & TV clips\",\"Film analysis & criticism\",\"Literature & writing craft\"],\"tags\":[\"solaris\",\"tarkovsky\",\"science fiction\",\"film\",\"stanislaw lem\"],\"quote\":\"the film's a masterpiece that I highly recommend\",\"recommenders\":2,\"score\":3.0},{\"vid\":\"ZBtMbBPzqHY\",\"title\":\"Navy pilots describe encounters with UFOs\",\"channel\":\"60 Minutes\",\"summary\":\"A 60 Minutes segment in which Navy pilots describe encounters with unidentified aerial phenomena, ahead of a report due to Congress.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN commenters point to it as eyewitness testimony and multi-radar evidence in UFO threads, though some dispute it.\",\"content_type\":\"news\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"unidentified aerial phenomena\",\"categories\":[\"Media, journalism & propaganda\",\"Military history & warfare\"],\"tags\":[\"ufo\",\"uap\",\"navy pilots\",\"60 minutes\",\"radar\"],\"quote\":\"At least watch this 60 Minutes short piece about this phenomenon\",\"recommenders\":2,\"score\":3.0}",
    ",{\"vid\":\"ZC5Zr3NC2PY\",\"title\":\"The Best Easy Way to Capture Analog Video (it's a little weird)\",\"channel\":\"Technology Connections\",\"summary\":\"Technology Connections shows a cheap method for capturing analog video: a composite-to-HDMI upscaler feeding an HDMI capture dongle, aimed at digitizing home movies and VHS tapes.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN people recommend it as an affordable, good-quality way to digitize analog video.\",\"content_type\":\"tutorial\",\"level\":\"intro\",\"primary_topic\":\"analog video capture\",\"categories\":[\"Audio & video engineering\",\"Consumer devices & gadgets\"],\"tags\":[\"vhs digitizing\",\"composite video\",\"hdmi capture\",\"home movies\",\"upscaler\"],\"quote\":\"does some good coverage of capturing/converting analogue video - hardware choices make huge difference.\",\"recommenders\":3,\"score\":3.0},{\"vid\":\"ZCmnQR3_qWg\",\"title\":\"35C3 -  The year in post-quantum crypto\",\"channel\":\"media.ccc.de\",\"summary\":\"Daniel J. Bernstein and Tanja Lange survey recent highlights in post-quantum cryptography at 35C3, covering the NIST competition, network protocol experiments, and broken candidates.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN recommends it as a good overview of the NIST candidates and the state of post-quantum crypto.\",\"content_type\":\"talk\",\"level\":\"advanced\",\"primary_topic\":\"post-quantum cryptography\",\"categories\":[\"Cryptography\",\"Quantum computing\"],\"tags\":[\"post-quantum\",\"nist competition\",\"djb\",\"cryptography\",\"35c3\"],\"quote\":\"This talk by djb and Tanja Lange is a good overview of the NIST candidates and the current state of pqcrypto\",\"recommenders\":3,\"score\":3.0},{\"vid\":\"ZLWMQLMiTPk\",\"title\":\"Thank You For Your Feedback - Don't Say Velcro\",\"channel\":\"VELCRO® Brand\",\"summary\":\"Velcro's follow-up to its \\\"Don't Say Velcro\\\" ad responds to viewer feedback, with a humorous take on trademark usage and alternative names for hook and loop fasteners.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN recommends it as a delightful sequel to the original ad, brought up in threads on trademarks and the original campaign.\",\"content_type\":\"comedy\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"trademark advertising\",\"categories\":[\"Product, marketing & sales\",\"Satire & parody\"],\"tags\":[\"velcro\",\"trademark\",\"advertising\",\"hook and loop\",\"humor\"],\"quote\":\"it's hilarious and worth watching\",\"recommenders\":3,\"score\":3.0},{\"vid\":\"ZOzZ8R4gphE\",\"title\":\"Let's port Diablo to SerenityOS!\",\"channel\":\"Andreas Kling\",\"summary\":\"Andreas Kling ports the game Diablo to SerenityOS, his from-scratch Unix-like operating system, using the devilutionX project. The roughly 80-minute session shows what porting third-party software to the OS involves.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN commenters recommend it as a demonstration of SerenityOS's hackability and fast iteration across all layers of the system.\",\"content_type\":\"demo\",\"level\":\"intermediate\",\"primary_topic\":\"operating system development\",\"categories\":[\"Operating systems & kernels\",\"Software practice, open source & careers\",\"C, C++, Rust, Go & systems languages\"],\"tags\":[\"serenityos\",\"andreas kling\",\"porting\",\"c++\",\"diablo\",\"os hacking\"],\"quote\":\"the video on porting Diablo to SerenityOS in an hour is pretty interesting to watch\",\"recommenders\":2,\"score\":3.0},{\"vid\":\"ZQc9-seU-5k\",\"title\":\"\\\"Swift as C++ Successor in FoundationDB\\\" by Konrad Malawski (Strange Loop 2023)\",\"channel\":\"Strange Loop Conference\",\"summary\":\"Konrad Malawski's Strange Loop 2023 talk shows how the FoundationDB team adopted Swift incrementally in a C++ codebase. It covers Swift's C++ interoperability, which let them move single functions or entire types over one at a time.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN commenters recommend it as the main resource on Swift as an incremental successor to C++ and on how the interoperability works in practice.\",\"content_type\":\"talk\",\"level\":\"advanced\",\"primary_topic\":\"swift c++ interoperability\",\"categories\":[\"C, C++, Rust, Go & systems languages\",\"Databases & storage\",\"Programming language design\"],\"tags\":[\"swift\",\"c++\",\"foundationdb\",\"interop\",\"incremental migration\",\"strange loop\"],\"quote\":\"The fairly recent presentation about starting to move FoundationDB to Swift[0] was also very interesting.\",\"recommenders\":3,\"score\":3.0},{\"vid\":\"ZRV3pBuPxEQ\",\"title\":\"PHP doesn't suck (anymore)\",\"channel\":\"Aaron Francis\",\"summary\":\"Aaron Francis walks through how PHP has changed from 2012 to 2023, covering traits, array destructuring, generators, typed properties and more. It is a quick chaptered tour of modern PHP features.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN commenters share it to show that modern PHP is much better than its reputation.\",\"content_type\":\"explainer\",\"level\":\"intro\",\"primary_topic\":\"modern php\",\"categories\":[\"Python, Ruby & scripting languages\",\"Web development\"],\"tags\":[\"php\",\"language features\",\"php 8\",\"web development\"],\"quote\":\"I was quite surprised to see how far PHP has come since I used it many years ago\",\"recommenders\":3,\"score\":3.0},{\"vid\":\"ZSPkcpGmflE\",\"title\":\"50 Years Ago, This Was a Wasteland. He Changed Everything | Short Film Showcase\",\"channel\":\"National Geographic\",\"summary\":\"An 8-minute National Geographic short film about David Bamberger, who bought 5,500 overgrazed acres in the Texas Hill Country and restored the land and its aquifers over about 50 years.\",\"why_hn\":\"Cited in climate and water threads as an encouraging example of large-scale landscape restoration.\",\"content_type\":\"documentary\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"land restoration\",\"categories\":[\"Environment, agriculture & food systems\",\"Documentaries & storytelling\"],\"tags\":[\"texas hill country\",\"aquifers\",\"conservation\",\"selah ranch\",\"water management\"],\"quote\":\"National Geographic did a really good 8-minute video on it\",\"recommenders\":3,\"score\":3.0},{\"vid\":\"ZUG9qYTJMsI\",\"title\":\"DollarShaveClub.com - Our Blades Are F***ing Great\",\"channel\":\"Dollar Shave Club\",\"summary\":\"Dollar Shave Club's low-budget launch ad, in which the founder jokes his way through the case for cheap mail-order razors.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN holds it up as a great example of a funny, viral company video that frames the razor market well.\",\"content_type\":\"comedy\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"viral marketing video\",\"categories\":[\"Product, marketing & sales\",\"Startups & entrepreneurship\"],\"tags\":[\"dollar shave club\",\"advertising\",\"startup marketing\",\"viral video\",\"razors\"],\"quote\":\"is absolutely amazing for how low budget it is\",\"recommenders\":3,\"score\":3.0},{\"vid\":\"ZerUbHmuY04\",\"title\":\"Causal understanding of water displacement by a crow\",\"channel\":\"PLOS Media\",\"summary\":\"A silent PLOS ONE video of New Caledonian crows solving Aesop's Fable puzzles by dropping objects to raise water and reach food. It shows example trials from experiments testing causal understanding of water displacement.\",\"why_hn\":\"Used as vivid evidence of crow intelligence and animal physical reasoning in discussions of cognition.\",\"content_type\":\"demo\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"crow intelligence\",\"categories\":[\"Animals & nature\",\"Psychology & human behavior\"],\"tags\":[\"crows\",\"animal cognition\",\"water displacement\",\"tool use\",\"aesop's fable\"],\"quote\":\"This video is a startling verification.of the crows mental capabilities.\",\"recommenders\":3,\"score\":3.0},{\"vid\":\"_7X6Yeydgyg\",\"title\":\"POLYBIUS - The Video Game That Doesn't Exist\",\"channel\":\"Ahoy\",\"summary\":\"A 69-minute documentary on the Polybius arcade-game legend. It examines visual, physical and anecdotal evidence, traces the story's source, and concludes the game never existed beyond one website entry.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN rates it among the best gaming video essays and Ahoy as one of the best creators on the platform.\",\"content_type\":\"documentary\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"polybius arcade legend\",\"categories\":[\"Game history & retro gaming\",\"Documentaries & storytelling\",\"Internet culture & memes\"],\"tags\":[\"polybius\",\"urban legend\",\"arcade games\",\"video essay\",\"retro gaming\"],\"quote\":\"the best gaming-related video essay produced!\",\"recommenders\":2,\"score\":3.0},{\"vid\":\"_9B__0S21y8\",\"title\":\"\\\"Tackling Concurrency Bugs with TLA+\\\" by Hillel Wayne\",\"channel\":\"Strange Loop Conference\",\"summary\":\"Hillel Wayne's Strange Loop talk introducing TLA+ as a specification language for finding concurrency bugs in designs. It covers stalling, race conditions and dropped messages, with PlusCal examples.\",\"why_hn\":\"Recommended as a concise, high-level intro to what TLA+ is and when it helps.\",\"content_type\":\"talk\",\"level\":\"intro\",\"primary_topic\":\"formal specification with tla+\",\"categories\":[\"Logic & formal methods\",\"Distributed systems\"],\"tags\":[\"tla+\",\"concurrency\",\"pluscal\",\"formal methods\",\"hillel wayne\"],\"quote\":\"If you are new to TLA+ and just want to get the basic idea and use cases, I recommend the talk.\",\"recommenders\":3,\"score\":3.0},{\"vid\":\"_KRb_qV9P4g\",\"title\":\"Smoother animation ≠ Better animation [read pinned comment]\",\"channel\":\"Noodle\",\"summary\":\"Animator Noodle explains why frame interpolation does not make animation better, covering timing, easing, smear frames and using the wrong tool for the job. A pinned correction says the video is partly outdated given later AI developments.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN commenters recommend it in motion-smoothing and interpolation threads as an overview of why interpolation hurts animation.\",\"content_type\":\"explainer\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"frame interpolation in animation\",\"categories\":[\"Animation & visual effects\"],\"tags\":[\"animation\",\"motion smoothing\",\"frame interpolation\",\"timing and easing\",\"anime\"],\"quote\":\"A really good video on the subject\",\"recommenders\":4,\"score\":3.0},{\"vid\":\"_fQtxKmgJC8\",\"title\":\"The Story of Tetris\",\"channel\":\"Gaming Historian\",\"summary\":\"Gaming Historian recounts how Alexey Pajitnov created Tetris in the Soviet Union and how a fight over publishing rights spanned the West, Mirrorsoft, Nintendo and the Cold War. It runs about an hour with chaptered parts.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN recommends it as an excellent documentary on Tetris and its tangled licensing history.\",\"content_type\":\"documentary\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"history of tetris\",\"categories\":[\"Game history & retro gaming\",\"Tech company stories & documentaries\"],\"tags\":[\"tetris\",\"video game history\",\"licensing\",\"soviet union\",\"nintendo\"],\"quote\":\"excellent and fascinating documentary on the history of Tetris\",\"recommenders\":4,\"score\":3.0},{\"vid\":\"_o7qjN3KF8U\",\"title\":\"The Hustle\",\"channel\":\"KRAZAM\",\"summary\":\"A KRAZAM satirical sketch about hustle culture and productivity obsession in tech.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN posts it as a joke in productivity and focus threads, and some praise the channel as pitch-perfect satire of tech stereotypes.\",\"content_type\":\"comedy\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"tech satire\",\"categories\":[\"Satire & parody\",\"Startups & entrepreneurship\"],\"tags\":[\"hustle culture\",\"krazam\",\"productivity\",\"satire\",\"startup humor\"],\"quote\":\"such a pitch perfect shot at a very common person in tech\",\"recommenders\":3,\"score\":3.0},{\"vid\":\"_x0eyNkNpL0\",\"title\":\"Violence | Slavoj Žižek | Talks at Google\",\"channel\":\"Talks at Google\",\"summary\":\"Slavoj Zizek discusses his book Violence in an Authors@Google talk in New York. He covers ideology, including his idea of the unknown knowns.\",\"why_hn\":\"Recommended as a relatively clear introduction to Zizek's thinking, especially his account of ideology and unknown knowns.\",\"content_type\":\"talk\",\"level\":\"intermediate\",\"primary_topic\":\"ideology and violence\",\"categories\":[\"Philosophy & ethics\"],\"tags\":[\"slavoj zizek\",\"ideology\",\"philosophy\",\"unknown knowns\",\"authors at google\"],\"quote\":\"when it comes to discussing ideology, he's doing the best outreach bar none.\",\"recommenders\":4,\"score\":3.0},{\"vid\":\"a9b9IYqsb_U\",\"title\":\"Howard Payne & Deviant Ollam  - This Key is Your Key, This Key is My Key\",\"channel\":\"DeviantOllam\",\"summary\":\"A HOPE conference talk by Howard Payne and Deviant Ollam on common keys, such as elevator and fire service keys, that open many buildings. It covers physical security weaknesses from shared key standards.\",\"why_hn\":\"Brought up in threads on elevators and locks as an engaging talk on common keys.\",\"content_type\":\"talk\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"physical security keys\",\"categories\":[\"Security & hacking\",\"Hacker culture & free software\"],\"tags\":[\"elevator keys\",\"locks\",\"fire keys\",\"physical security\",\"hope\"],\"quote\":\"I have to also mention another video of theirs\",\"recommenders\":3,\"score\":3.0},{\"vid\":\"aICaAEXDJQQ\",\"title\":\"The Insane Engineering of James Webb Telescope\",\"channel\":\"Real Engineering\",\"summary\":\"Real Engineering explains the engineering behind the James Webb Space Telescope, including its folding mirror, sunshield, orbit and cooling systems, and why deployment was so difficult.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN recommends it as an accessible in-depth explanation of how Webb works and why its deployment was remarkable.\",\"content_type\":\"explainer\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"james webb space telescope\",\"categories\":[\"Space exploration & spaceflight\",\"Mechanical & precision engineering\"],\"tags\":[\"jwst\",\"space engineering\",\"telescope deployment\",\"cryocooler\",\"nasa\"],\"quote\":\"For some context around what makes this deployment so remarkable, watch this[0] video\",\"recommenders\":3,\"score\":3.0},{\"vid\":\"aIx2N-viNwY\",\"title\":\"Why Life Seems to Speed Up as We Age\",\"channel\":\"Veritasium\",\"summary\":\"Veritasium explores why time seems to speed up as we age, covering chronoception and several competing explanations beyond the common proportional-theory argument.\",\"why_hn\":\"Cited in threads about perceived time as a good, detailed explanation of the effect.\",\"content_type\":\"explainer\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"time perception\",\"categories\":[\"Psychology & human behavior\",\"Neuroscience & the brain\"],\"tags\":[\"chronoception\",\"aging\",\"psychology\",\"veritasium\",\"perception\"],\"quote\":\"Veritasium explores this and IMO the alternative arguments are more compelling\",\"recommenders\":4,\"score\":3.0},{\"vid\":\"aP0Y1uAA-2Y\",\"title\":\"Stanford Seminar: Beyond Floating Point: Next Generation Computer Arithmetic\",\"channel\":\"Stanford Online\",\"summary\":\"John Gustafson presents posits, a proposed drop-in replacement for IEEE 754 floats that is simpler in hardware and more flexible in precision. The seminar includes a live demo and machine learning results.\",\"why_hn\":\"Cited in floating-point threads as the main introduction to posits and unums as an alternative to IEEE floats.\",\"content_type\":\"lecture\",\"level\":\"advanced\",\"primary_topic\":\"computer arithmetic posits\",\"categories\":[\"Computer architecture & CPUs\",\"Pure mathematics\",\"Machine learning & deep learning\"],\"tags\":[\"posits\",\"unum\",\"floating point\",\"ieee 754\",\"numerical computing\"],\"quote\":\"Here's a nice introductory presentation\",\"recommenders\":5,\"score\":3.0},{\"vid\":\"aVUqaB0IMh4\",\"title\":\"KiCad 6 STM32 PCB Design Full Tutorial - Phil's Lab #65\",\"channel\":\"Phil’s Lab\",\"summary\":\"A 100-minute tutorial from Phil's Lab on designing an STM32-based 'black pill' PCB in KiCad 6. It covers schematic capture, two-layer layout and routing, USB, and sending the board for manufacture and assembly.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN recommends it as a practical way to learn KiCad and PCB design by following one full project.\",\"content_type\":\"tutorial\",\"level\":\"intermediate\",\"primary_topic\":\"pcb design\",\"categories\":[\"Electronics & circuit design\",\"Embedded systems & DIY electronics\"],\"tags\":[\"kicad\",\"stm32\",\"pcb layout\",\"schematic\",\"hardware design\"],\"quote\":\"The Youtube channel Phil's Lab has a really good series\",\"recommenders\":3,\"score\":3.0},{\"vid\":\"aXQ2lO3ieBA\",\"title\":\"Pentagon Wars - Bradley Fighting Vehicle Evolution\",\"channel\":\"66NOVA66\",\"summary\":\"A roughly ten-minute scene from the movie The Pentagon Wars showing how the Bradley Fighting Vehicle's requirements ballooned through committee demands into a compromised design. It is a satirical dramatization of military procurement.\",\"why_hn\":\"Linked in nearly every F-35 or procurement thread as the classic illustration of feature creep and design by stakeholder committee, including in software.\",\"content_type\":\"comedy\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"feature creep in procurement\",\"categories\":[\"Film & TV clips\",\"Military history & warfare\",\"Satire & parody\"],\"tags\":[\"pentagon wars\",\"bradley\",\"feature creep\",\"f-35\",\"requirements\",\"satire\"],\"quote\":\"It's a great example of how trying to design a product that works well for every stakeholder in every scenario leads to a Frankenstein of a product\",\"recommenders\":3,\"score\":3.0},{\"vid\":\"aXflBZXAucQ\",\"title\":\"Why We Sleep: Science of Sleep & Dreams | Matthew Walker | Talks at Google\",\"channel\":\"Talks at Google\",\"summary\":\"Berkeley sleep scientist Matthew Walker presents the science of sleep and dreams and how sleep affects health and lifespan, based on his book Why We Sleep.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN suggests it as an easy alternative to the book for people who want Walker's sleep findings.\",\"content_type\":\"talk\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"sleep science\",\"categories\":[\"Fitness, sleep & longevity\",\"Neuroscience & the brain\"],\"tags\":[\"sleep\",\"matthew walker\",\"dreams\",\"health\",\"sleep deprivation\"],\"quote\":\"that I recommend watching if you're not a book person\",\"recommenders\":3,\"score\":3.0},{\"vid\":\"aY985qzn7oI\",\"title\":\"harvard & aliens & crackpots: a disambiguation of Avi Loeb\",\"channel\":\"Angela Collier \",\"summary\":\"Physicist Angela Collier gives an hour-long critique of Avi Loeb's alien claims and reputation, placing them within the broader topic of physics crackpots. The Loeb discussion starts around the 24 minute mark.\",\"why_hn\":\"Frequently linked as an in-depth, well-presented skeptical take whenever Loeb's alien claims come up.\",\"content_type\":\"commentary\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"avi loeb and alien claims\",\"categories\":[\"Cosmology & astrophysics\",\"Scientific method & science communication\"],\"tags\":[\"avi loeb\",\"oumuamua\",\"crackpots\",\"seti\",\"science skepticism\"],\"quote\":\"I was surprised about myself that I watched the entire thing and I guess it's because of the high quality of the presentation\",\"recommenders\":5,\"score\":3.0},{\"vid\":\"agS6ZXBrcng\",\"title\":\"HBO Intro - Behind the Scenes\",\"channel\":\"archivefilms\",\"summary\":\"A 1983 behind-the-scenes film about making the HBO 'Feature Presentation' starship logo sequence. It shows the handcrafted miniature city, motion-control cameras and practical effects.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN recommends it as a look at pre-CGI effects work that looks like CGI but was entirely physical.\",\"content_type\":\"documentary\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"practical visual effects\",\"categories\":[\"Animation & visual effects\",\"Filmmaking & video production\"],\"tags\":[\"hbo intro\",\"miniatures\",\"motion control\",\"pre-cgi\",\"film history\"],\"quote\":\"looks CGI but is entirely physical models, motion controlled cameras, and clever compositing\",\"recommenders\":3,\"score\":3.0},{\"vid\":\"b0EF0VTs9Dc\",\"title\":\"Monads and Gonads\",\"channel\":\"Google TechTalks\",\"summary\":\"Douglas Crockford's Google Tech Talk explains monads without category theory or Haskell, implementing them in JavaScript and tying them to Ajax and promises. He also touches on odd asides such as coloring code by scope.\",\"why_hn\":\"Often recommended as a demystifying monad talk in plain JavaScript, though some find it light on definitions.\",\"content_type\":\"talk\",\"level\":\"intermediate\",\"primary_topic\":\"monads in javascript\",\"categories\":[\"Functional programming\",\"Web development\"],\"tags\":[\"monads\",\"javascript\",\"douglas crockford\",\"functional programming\",\"promises\"],\"quote\":\"what I thought to be one of DC's greatest talks\",\"recommenders\":2,\"score\":3.0},{\"vid\":\"b9FC9fAlfQE\",\"title\":\"EEVblog #186 - Soldering Tutorial Part 3 - Surface Mount\",\"channel\":\"EEVblog\",\"summary\":\"Dave Jones of EEVblog shows hand soldering of surface-mount parts, including drag soldering and tack-and-reflow of 0.5mm fine-pitch ICs, with solder paste and hot air.\",\"why_hn\":\"Recommended as a good introduction to SMD soldering techniques for beginners.\",\"content_type\":\"tutorial\",\"level\":\"intro\",\"primary_topic\":\"smd soldering\",\"categories\":[\"Repair, teardowns & right to repair\",\"Electronics & circuit design\"],\"tags\":[\"soldering\",\"surface mount\",\"drag soldering\",\"hot air\",\"electronics\"],\"quote\":\"Check out Dave Jones' multi-part videos on soldering\",\"recommenders\":3,\"score\":3.0},{\"vid\":\"bAUVCn_jw5I\",\"title\":\"Why Starting A Rocket Engine Is So Hard!\",\"channel\":\"Everyday Astronaut\",\"summary\":\"Tim Dodd's hour-long deep dive on how rocket engines start, from solid motors to liquid engines. It covers thermal conditioning, spin-up, ignition methods, starting in space, and a step-by-step RS-25 startup.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN recommends it as the best explanation of why engine start is hard and what can go wrong.\",\"content_type\":\"explainer\",\"level\":\"intermediate\",\"primary_topic\":\"rocket engine ignition\",\"categories\":[\"Space exploration & spaceflight\",\"Mechanical & precision engineering\"],\"tags\":[\"rocket engines\",\"ignition\",\"rs-25\",\"everyday astronaut\",\"propulsion\"],\"quote\":\"Here's a 1hr video from the Everyday Astronaut explaining the process and everything that can go wrong.\",\"recommenders\":3,\"score\":3.0},{\"vid\":\"bL6hp8BKB24\",\"title\":\"Why CG Sucks (Except It Doesn't)\",\"channel\":\"RocketJump Film School\",\"summary\":\"RocketJump Film School argues that we only notice bad CG while great CG is invisible, so CG seems to be everywhere ruining movies when it often is not.\",\"why_hn\":\"Used as a counterpoint whenever commenters claim CGI always looks fake.\",\"content_type\":\"commentary\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"visual effects perception\",\"categories\":[\"Animation & visual effects\",\"Filmmaking & video production\"],\"tags\":[\"cgi\",\"vfx\",\"film\",\"uncanny valley\"],\"quote\":\"This video from a few years ago is a great counterpoint\",\"recommenders\":3,\"score\":3.0},{\"vid\":\"bfN2JWifLCY\",\"title\":\"Why lockdowns are the wrong policy: Swedish expert Prof. Johan Giesecke\",\"channel\":\"UnHerd\",\"summary\":\"UnHerd interview with Swedish epidemiologist Johan Giesecke, who explains why he thinks lockdowns are the wrong policy and describes Sweden's approach during the spring 2020 pandemic.\",\"why_hn\":\"Commenters point to it for the Swedish insider perspective on lockdowns, with some later calling its statements prescient.\",\"content_type\":\"interview\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"covid-19 lockdown policy\",\"categories\":[\"Medicine & infectious disease\",\"Politics & history (other)\"],\"tags\":[\"sweden\",\"epidemiology\",\"herd immunity\",\"lockdowns\",\"covid-19\"],\"quote\":\"Here's an interesting interview with a senior epidemiologist partly responsible for Sweden's unconventional strategy\",\"recommenders\":7,\"score\":3.0},{\"vid\":\"boPEO2auJj4\",\"title\":\"CppCon 2015: Timur Doumler “C++ in the Audio Industry”\",\"channel\":\"CppCon\",\"summary\":\"Timur Doumler's CppCon 2015 talk on how C++ is used in the audio industry. It covers the patterns and tools audio developers rely on, including handling real-time constraints.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN commenters recommend it as an introduction to real-time and low-latency programming in C++ for people getting into audio.\",\"content_type\":\"talk\",\"level\":\"intermediate\",\"primary_topic\":\"real-time audio programming\",\"categories\":[\"C, C++, Rust, Go & systems languages\",\"Information theory & signal processing\"],\"tags\":[\"c++\",\"audio\",\"real-time\",\"dsp\",\"cppcon\"],\"quote\":\"he goes through real time strategies to keep the response time under around 30ms IIRC\",\"recommenders\":3,\"score\":3.0},{\"vid\":\"bvim4rsNHkQ\",\"title\":\"How Not to Land an Orbital Rocket Booster\",\"channel\":\"SpaceX\",\"summary\":\"SpaceX's own compilation of failed orbital booster landing attempts, set to sound, showing the crashes before landings succeeded.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN uses it as evidence that SpaceX iterated through visible failures and is open and humorous about them.\",\"content_type\":\"other\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"rocket landing failures\",\"categories\":[\"Space exploration & spaceflight\"],\"tags\":[\"spacex\",\"falcon 9\",\"booster landing\",\"iteration\",\"failure montage\"],\"quote\":\"you might enjoy this official SpaceX Blooper reel from 2017 that shows the numerous spectacular failures that they worked through.\",\"recommenders\":4,\"score\":3.0},{\"vid\":\"c1UBJbfR-H0\",\"title\":\"\\\"Compacting the Uncompactable\\\" by Bobby Powers\",\"channel\":\"Strange Loop Conference\",\"summary\":\"Bobby Powers presents Mesh, a drop-in malloc replacement that eliminates memory fragmentation in unmodified C/C++ programs by compacting memory. The talk covers how it works despite C's fixed object addresses, and its benefits for programs like Redis.\",\"why_hn\":\"Recommended as a great talk on solving fragmentation for C/C++ and runtimes like Ruby and Python without code changes.\",\"content_type\":\"talk\",\"level\":\"advanced\",\"primary_topic\":\"memory allocation\",\"categories\":[\"C, C++, Rust, Go & systems languages\",\"Software performance & optimization\"],\"tags\":[\"malloc\",\"memory fragmentation\",\"compaction\",\"mesh\",\"c++\"],\"quote\":\"There was a great talk at Strange Loop about a drop-in malloc replacement which compacts.\",\"recommenders\":3,\"score\":3.0},{\"vid\":\"c2lgEyNaop4\",\"title\":\"Classic Game Postmortem: Alone in the Dark\",\"channel\":\"GDC Festival of Gaming\",\"summary\":\"Frederick Raynal gives a GDC postmortem of Alone in the Dark, the game that helped create the survival horror genre. He covers how the team built it and shows some of the old tools used.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN commenters recommend it as a firsthand account from the creator, including the old tooling.\",\"content_type\":\"talk\",\"level\":\"intermediate\",\"primary_topic\":\"game development history\",\"categories\":[\"Game history & retro gaming\",\"Game design\",\"Game programming & engines\"],\"tags\":[\"alone in the dark\",\"postmortem\",\"survival horror\",\"gdc\",\"3d games\"],\"quote\":\"There is a very nice presentation [1] in which Raynal shows some of the old tools that were used to create Alone in the Dark.\",\"recommenders\":3,\"score\":3.0},{\"vid\":\"cQO2XTP7QDw\",\"title\":\"I sent robot forgeries to a handwriting expert\",\"channel\":\"Stuff Made Here\",\"summary\":\"Stuff Made Here builds a handwriting robot and sends its output to a handwriting expert to see whether it can pass as forgery. It walks through the engineering trials and errors along the way.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN commenters recommend it as the physical-machine take on replicating handwriting, with plenty of explained iteration.\",\"content_type\":\"demo\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"handwriting robots\",\"categories\":[\"Robotics\",\"3D printing, CNC & maker projects\",\"Mechanical & precision engineering\"],\"tags\":[\"pen plotter\",\"handwriting\",\"forgery\",\"robotics\",\"engineering\"],\"quote\":\"really cool video by Stuff Made Here explaining how he tried to make 'realistic' handwritten forgeries with a pen plotter\",\"recommenders\":3,\"score\":3.0},{\"vid\":\"cQq2pKNDgIs\",\"title\":\"Unlocking UAP Mysteries: Economics, Aliens, and The Great Filter | Merged EP0109\",\"channel\":\"Merged Podcast\",\"summary\":\"A 146-minute Merged Podcast episode in which UAP researcher Ryan Graves talks with economist Robin Hanson about UFOs. Topics include the Great Filter, Hanson's grabby aliens model, and the push for more inquiry into UAPs.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN commenters point to it for Hanson's grabby aliens reasoning as an unusual framework for thinking about UFO behavior and intelligent life in the cosmos.\",\"content_type\":\"podcast\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"grabby aliens and ufos\",\"categories\":[\"Media, journalism & propaganda\",\"Cosmology & astrophysics\",\"Microeconomics & behavioral economics\"],\"tags\":[\"robin hanson\",\"grabby aliens\",\"great filter\",\"uap\",\"fermi paradox\"],\"quote\":\"Grabby Aliens concept by Robin Hanson is an interesting new take on UFOs.\",\"recommenders\":3,\"score\":3.0},{\"vid\":\"cTsEzmFamZ8\",\"title\":\"Joe Rogan Experience #1245 - Andrew Yang\",\"channel\":\"PowerfulJRE\",\"summary\":\"Joe Rogan's long interview with Andrew Yang during his 2020 presidential run. They discuss universal basic income, automation and his policy proposals.\",\"why_hn\":\"Suggested as a starting point for understanding Yang's capitalist case for UBI, though some note it is long and dated.\",\"content_type\":\"podcast\",\"level