s\",\"khan academy\",\"learning\",\"education research\",\"veritasium\"],\"quote\":\"please watch the whole video because it explains one massive problem with video science lessons and how to partially fix the problem.\",\"recommenders\":2,\"score\":3.0},{\"vid\":\"egEraZP9yXQ\",\"title\":\"How Many Holes Does a Human Have?\",\"channel\":\"Vsauce\",\"summary\":\"Vsauce asks how many holes a human has and uses topology to show the answer depends on what counts as a hole, with animations and expert input.\",\"why_hn\":\"Pointed to as a fun, light introduction to topology and to answer the human-holes question.\",\"content_type\":\"explainer\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"topology\",\"categories\":[\"Pure mathematics\",\"Recreational & visual math\"],\"tags\":[\"topology\",\"holes\",\"genus\",\"mathematics\",\"anatomy\"],\"quote\":\"If you'd like a fun, light, video introduction to this topic, this Vsauce video is worth a watch\",\"recommenders\":3,\"score\":3.0},{\"vid\":\"ez4DgdurRPg\",\"title\":\"Dance p 3 Mar09\",\"channel\":\"Geoff Cumming\",\"summary\":\"Geoff Cumming uses a simulation to show how wildly the p value varies from one replication to the next because of sampling variability. He argues for estimation and confidence intervals over null hypothesis significance testing.\",\"why_hn\":\"Recommended as a vivid visual demonstration of how unreliable p-values are.\",\"content_type\":\"explainer\",\"level\":\"intro\",\"primary_topic\":\"p-value variability\",\"categories\":[\"Data science & statistics\",\"Scientific method & science communication\"],\"tags\":[\"p-values\",\"nhst\",\"statistics\",\"estimation\",\"replication\"],\"quote\":\"absolutely fantastic and well worth watching\",\"recommenders\":2,\"score\":3.0},{\"vid\":\"f5SE47Xjx2Q\",\"title\":\"Why 50 Million Chinese Homes are Empty\",\"channel\":\"PolyMatter\",\"summary\":\"PolyMatter explains China's housing bubble and why around 50 million homes sit empty. It covers cultural and economic reasons behind the overbuilding and the government's bind.\",\"why_hn\":\"Recommended as a clear, compact explainer on China's empty homes, ghost cities and property troubles.\",\"content_type\":\"explainer\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"china housing bubble\",\"categories\":[\"Macroeconomics & financial crises\",\"Investing & personal finance\"],\"tags\":[\"china\",\"real estate\",\"ghost cities\",\"housing\",\"economics\"],\"quote\":\"it explains clearly (for a complex situation) what's been going on in China's real estate, the 'ghost cities' and the demolitions.\",\"recommenders\":3,\"score\":3.0},{\"vid\":\"f8ZqBLcIvw0\",\"title\":\"The Origins of Russian Authoritarianism\",\"channel\":\"Kraut\",\"summary\":\"Kraut traces centuries of political development, from Mongol rule and the Orthodox church to Muscovite autocracy, that shaped Russia's authoritarian state. It uses countryball animation and compares Russia with Europe and China.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN recommends it as a good introduction to Russian authoritarianism, though some commenters say it is flawed or wrong on many points.\",\"content_type\":\"explainer\",\"level\":\"intro\",\"primary_topic\":\"russian political history\",\"categories\":[\"World history\",\"Geopolitics & foreign policy\"],\"tags\":[\"russia\",\"authoritarianism\",\"mongol rule\",\"history\",\"countryballs\"],\"quote\":\"this video gives a good introduction to the origins of Russian Authoritarianism\",\"recommenders\":3,\"score\":3.0},{\"vid\":\"fD-R35DSSZY\",\"title\":\"The Longest Year in Human History (46 B.C.E.)\",\"channel\":\"Historia Civilis\",\"summary\":\"Historia Civilis tells the story of 46 BCE, the 445-day year in which Julius Caesar reformed the Roman calendar. It covers the political context, including the civil war, Cato and Cicero.\",\"why_hn\":\"Recommended as an entertaining and well-explained account of why our calendar looks the way it does.\",\"content_type\":\"explainer\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"roman calendar reform\",\"categories\":[\"World history\"],\"tags\":[\"julius caesar\",\"roman republic\",\"calendar\",\"ancient rome\",\"history\"],\"quote\":\"Historia Civilis has a great video explaining how Caeser used the longest year to his advantage in war\",\"recommenders\":4,\"score\":3.0},{\"vid\":\"fPrvnlvnu-k\",\"title\":\"TWiST #46 with David Heinemeier Hansson\",\"channel\":\"ThisWeekinStartups\",\"summary\":\"An episode of This Week in Startups in which Jason Calacanis interviews Ruby on Rails creator David Heinemeier Hansson. They discuss startups, bootstrapping and 37signals' approach to business.\",\"why_hn\":\"Recommended as an entertaining look at DHH's views and what the 37signals founders stand for.\",\"content_type\":\"interview\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"bootstrapping startups\",\"categories\":[\"Startups & entrepreneurship\",\"Tech pioneers & interviews\",\"Python, Ruby & scripting languages\"],\"tags\":[\"dhh\",\"37signals\",\"ruby on rails\",\"startups\",\"this week in startups\"],\"quote\":\"People, please watch these few videos to genuinely understand what 37Signal guys (David and Jason) stand for\",\"recommenders\":3,\"score\":3.0},{\"vid\":\"fW8amMCVAJQ\",\"title\":\"First Follower: Leadership Lessons from Dancing Guy\",\"channel\":\"Derek Sivers\",\"summary\":\"Derek Sivers annotates a short clip of a lone dancer at a festival, showing how a first follower turns a ridiculous act into a movement. He draws out lessons about leadership and making it easy to follow.\",\"why_hn\":\"A go-to short explanation of how movements start and why early followers matter.\",\"content_type\":\"explainer\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"leadership and movements\",\"categories\":[\"Management, leadership & organizations\",\"Psychology & human behavior\"],\"tags\":[\"first follower\",\"leadership\",\"derek sivers\",\"social movements\",\"tipping point\"],\"quote\":\"Watch this 2 minute to see how this works, you 