velopment\",\"Software architecture & design\"],\"tags\":[\"webassembly\",\"wasi\",\"component model\",\"composability\",\"sandboxing\"],\"quote\":\"I thought this keynote presentation[0] by Luke Wagner at Wasmcon was great and covered it very well.\",\"recommenders\":3,\"score\":3.0},{\"vid\":\"tMP5Pbx8I4s\",\"title\":\"Turning Waves Into Particles\",\"channel\":\"Huygens Optics\",\"summary\":\"Huygens Optics explores the idea that space is a non-linear elastic medium, and uses simulations to show how wave energy might be confined locally into particle-like objects. It touches on inertia, the Schwinger limit and the vacuum as a medium.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN commenters find the hypothesis elegant and the channel consistently thought-provoking, and point to it in threads on light, particles and wave functions.\",\"content_type\":\"explainer\",\"level\":\"advanced\",\"primary_topic\":\"nonlinear optics and particle models\",\"categories\":[\"Fundamental physics\",\"Quantum physics\",\"Everyday physics & science demos\"],\"tags\":[\"nonlinear vacuum\",\"schwinger limit\",\"wave simulation\",\"light and matter\",\"physics\"],\"quote\":\"the explanation is beautiful in its simplicity\",\"recommenders\":2,\"score\":3.0},{\"vid\":\"tTBWfkE7BXU\",\"title\":\"Noam Chomsky - Manufacturing Consent\",\"channel\":\"Chomsky's Philosophy\",\"summary\":\"A nine-minute excerpt from the 1992 documentary Manufacturing Consent in which Noam Chomsky summarizes how corporate media shapes public discourse.\",\"why_hn\":\"Cited as a short overview of the propaganda model whenever commenters discuss media influence and consent manufacturing.\",\"content_type\":\"documentary\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"media propaganda\",\"categories\":[\"Media, journalism & propaganda\",\"Documentaries & storytelling\"],\"tags\":[\"noam chomsky\",\"manufacturing consent\",\"propaganda model\",\"corporate media\",\"media literacy\"],\"quote\":\"Here's a clip from a documentary based on the book\"