he air.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN links it whenever airline route rules, cabotage or loopholes come up, as a concise background explainer.\",\"content_type\":\"explainer\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"aviation regulation\",\"categories\":[\"Aviation & aerospace engineering\",\"Geopolitics & foreign policy\"],\"tags\":[\"airlines\",\"five freedoms\",\"air treaties\",\"cabotage\",\"aviation economics\"],\"quote\":\"This video has a lot of good info on it\",\"recommenders\":3,\"score\":3.0},{\"vid\":\"tiKCORN-6m8\",\"title\":\"Why guitarists USED TO play more in tune! (Microtonal Frets)\",\"channel\":\"Brandon Acker\",\"summary\":\"Classical guitarist Brandon Acker shows how guitars with tied-on gut frets, as used 300 years ago, can play more in tune than modern fixed metal frets. He demonstrates microtonal and meantone tunings on a guitar with movable frets.\",\"why_hn\":\"Pointed to in tuning and temperament threads as an audible demonstration of how meantone differs from equal temperament.\",\"content_type\":\"demo\",\"level\":\"intermediate\",\"primary_topic\":\"guitar tuning systems\",\"categories\":[\"Music theory, synthesis & production\",\"Music performance & songs\"],\"tags\":[\"gut frets\",\"meantone\",\"microtonal\",\"temperament\",\"classical guitar\"],\"quote\":\"Brandon Acker gives a wonderful overview on the classical guitar\",\"recommenders\":3,\"score\":3.0},{\"vid\":\"tnBQmEqBCY0\",\"title\":\"Elon Musk : How to Build the Future\",\"channel\":\"Y Combinator\",\"summary\":\"A 20-minute Y Combinator interview in which Sam Altman asks Elon Musk how to build the future. Topics include which problems a 22-year-old should work on, such as AI, genetics, and brain interfaces, and general advice for founders.\",\"why_hn\":\"Offered as a more down-to-earth Musk interview with better questions than most, and cited for his stated concerns about concentrated AI power.\",\"content_type\":\"interview\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"entrepreneurship 