s\",\"arenas\",\"memory management\",\"systems programming\"],\"quote\":null,\"recommenders\":3,\"score\":3.0},{\"vid\":\"vKA4w2O61Xo\",\"title\":\"The Most Common Cognitive Bias\",\"channel\":\"Veritasium\",\"summary\":\"A Veritasium video that runs the 2-4-8 rule-guessing puzzle on people to show how they test only examples that confirm their hypothesis. It uses this to illustrate confirmation bias and falsification.\",\"why_hn\":\"Recommended as a clear demonstration of confirmation bias and the value of trying to break your own hypothesis.\",\"content_type\":\"explainer\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"confirmation bias\",\"categories\":[\"Psychology & human behavior\",\"Scientific method & science communication\"],\"tags\":[\"veritasium\",\"falsification\",\"scientific method\",\"2-4-8 puzzle\",\"cognitive bias\"],\"quote\":\"I would suggest this video by Veritasium, which also touches on this, at a very fundamental level\",\"recommenders\":3,\"score\":3.0},{\"vid\":\"vOvQCPLkPt4\",\"title\":\"Applied Sciences Group: High Performance Touch\",\"channel\":\"Microsoft Research\",\"summary\":\"A Microsoft Research demo from TechFest 2012 of a lab touch system that lets viewers feel the effect of different input latencies, down to about 1 ms. It shows how much more responsive dragging feels compared with typical 100 ms touch delay.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN commenters cite it whenever input latency comes up, as the demonstration that people can perceive touch delay down to 1 ms.\",\"content_type\":\"demo\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"touch input latency\",\"categories\":[\"GUI, HCI & interface history\",\"UX & UI design\",\"Consumer devices & gadgets\"],\"tags\":[\"latency\",\"touchscreens\",\"human-computer interaction\",\"microsoft research\",\"responsiveness\"],\"quote\":\"It shows the difference between from >100ms to ~1ms. It's mind baffling.\",\"recommenders\":3,\"score\":3.0},{\"vid\":\"vWkgEddb4-A\",\"title\":\"Introduction to Julia - Part 1