velopers.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN recommends it as a sampling of truly different programming paradigms beyond mainstream OOP.\",\"content_type\":\"talk\",\"level\":\"intermediate\",\"primary_topic\":\"programming language paradigms\",\"categories\":[\"Programming language design\",\"Functional programming\",\"Databases & storage\"],\"tags\":[\"sql\",\"prolog\",\"ml\",\"smalltalk\",\"language design\"],\"quote\":\"Check out this fantastic talk by Scott Wlaschin to get a sampling of truly different language paradigms\",\"recommenders\":2,\"score\":2.5},{\"vid\":\"0jI-AlWEwYI\",\"title\":\"Alexis King -  “Effects for Less” @ ZuriHac 2020\",\"channel\":\"Zürich Friends of Haskell\",\"summary\":\"Alexis King's ZuriHac 2020 talk on how effect systems in Haskell can be implemented efficiently. It looks at the performance cost of effect libraries and how to reduce it.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN commenters call it among the best talks of 2020 for understanding Haskell effect systems.\",\"content_type\":\"talk\",\"level\":\"advanced\",\"primary_topic\":\"haskell effect systems\",\"categories\":[\"Functional programming\",\"Software performance & optimization\"],\"tags\":[\"haskell\",\"effects\",\"performance\",\"functional programming\",\"alexis king\"],\"quote\":\"the best one I did watch this year was Alexis King's 'Effects for Less' (Haskell).\",\"recommenders\":2,\"score\":2.5},{\"vid\":\"0lJKucu6HJc\",\"title\":\"Sam Altman - How to Succeed with a Startup\",\"channel\":\"Y Combinator\",\"summary\":\"A 16-minute Y Combinator Startup School talk in which Sam Altman lays out what makes a startup succeed. It covers building a product people tell friends about, exponential markets, real versus fake trends, and having an ambitious vision.\",\"why_hn\":\"Recommended as the single Startup School video worth watching, a short and dense talk on what makes a startup work; one commenter dismisses it as platitudes.\",\"content_type\":\"talk\",\"level\":\"intro\",\"primary_topic\":\"startup success\