ust how brittle the whole thing is even behind the scenes\",\"recommenders\":2,\"score\":2.5},{\"vid\":\"A9U5wK_boYM\",\"title\":\"How I Fixed a 10 Year Old Guitar Hero Bug Without the Source Code\",\"channel\":\"ExileLord\",\"summary\":\"A reverse engineer walks through fixing a ten-year-old bug in Guitar Hero III without access to its source code, using a disassembler and decompiler. It is technical but explained step by step.\",\"why_hn\":\"Held up as a favorite tech talk and a great hard-debugging story about patching a game binary.\",\"content_type\":\"talk\",\"level\":\"intermediate\",\"primary_topic\":\"reverse engineering game bugs\",\"categories\":[\"Speedrunning, glitches & game hacking\",\"Security & hacking\",\"Testing, debugging & developer tools\"],\"tags\":[\"reverse engineering\",\"guitar hero\",\"ida\",\"x86\",\"debugging\",\"game hacking\"],\"quote\":\"One of the best though, for me, has to be this one on fixing a Guitar Hero bug\",\"recommenders\":2,\"score\":2.5},{\"vid\":\"AGUwcs9qJXY\",\"title\":\"Holy Post -  Race in America\",\"channel\":\"Holy Post Media\",\"summary\":\"Phil Vischer of VeggieTales and Holy Post gives an 18-minute history of racial injustice in America, covering why anger persists despite civil rights laws. It is told from an evangelical Christian perspective and adapted from a class he co-taught.\",\"why_hn\":\"Recommended as a concise, broad-strokes history of racial injustice, including the lasting effects of redlining.\",\"content_type\":\"explainer\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"history of racial injustice in america\",\"categories\":[\"Social issues & culture\",\"World history\",\"Religion, belief & skepticism\"],\"tags\":[\"race\",\"redlining\",\"civil rights\",\"us history\",\"christian perspective\"],\"quote\":\"There’s a great 18-minute video from Bob the Tomato, AKA Phil Vischer, which lays out the sordid history in broad detail.\",\"recommenders\":2,\"score\":2.5},{\"vid\":\"AJgY9FtDLbs\",\"title\":\"Rocker Jack White - Serious Jibber-Jabber with Conan O'Brien | Team Coco\",\"channel\":\"Team Coco\",\"summary\":\"Conan O'Brien interviews Jack White in a Serious Jibber-Jabber episode shot on 35mm film. They discuss White's creative process, his use of constraints and his approach to music and art.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN recommends it as an inspiring interview about passion, minimalism and deliberately imposing restrictions on creative work.\",\"content_type\":\"interview\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"creative constraints in music\",\"categories\":[\"Music performance & songs\",\"Tech pioneers & interviews\",\"Stand-up & sketch comedy\"],\"tags\":[\"jack white\",\"conan o'brien\",\"creativity\",\"constraints\",\"music\"],\"quote\":\"I highly recommend the interview with Conan\",\"recommenders\":2,\"score\":2.5},{\"vid\":\"AtPA6nIBs5g\",\"title\":\"Back to the Future | VFXcool (1/2)\",\"channel\":\"Captain Disillusion\",\"summary\":\"Captain Disillusion explains the visual effects behind the Back to the Future trilogy. He covers ILM's motion-control, computer-controlled camera work and clever pre-CGI tricks.\",\"why_hn\":\"Recommended as a succinct documentary on motion control and practical-effects ingenuity.\",\"content_type\":\"explainer\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"visual effects history\",\"categories\":[\"Animation & visual effects\",\"Film analysis & criticism\"],\"tags\":[\"vfx\",\"back to the future\",\"motion control\",\"ilm\",\"practical effects\"],\"quote\":\"is a really good yet succinct documentary on it\",\"recommenders\":2,\"score\":2.5},{\"vid\":\"B5FxFfymI4g\",\"title\":\"Disruptive Innovation - Clayton Christensen (Part 2)\",\"channel\":\"modplanman\",\"summary\":\"Clayton Christensen explains disruptive innovation using the steel industry, showing how mini-mills beat incumbents from the low end. He argues disruption is not about stupid or bad management.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN recommends it as an amazing, clear explanation of 