ategories\":[\"Transit, cities & urban planning\",\"Cars, EVs & motorcycles\"],\"tags\":[\"microcars\",\"amsterdam\",\"canta\",\"accessibility\",\"urban planning\"],\"quote\":\"Please, please watch the videos I linked.\",\"recommenders\":2,\"score\":2.5},{\"vid\":\"BBwepkVurCI\",\"title\":\"Charlie Brooker's Screenwipe - Reality TV Editing\",\"channel\":\"Samusek TDS\",\"summary\":\"A clip from Charlie Brooker's BBC show Screenwipe showing how reality TV uses editing to manufacture emotion and narrative. It demonstrates how the same footage can be cut to give very different impressions.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN people cite it as a vivid demonstration of how editing shapes perception in documentaries and reality television.\",\"content_type\":\"commentary\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"reality tv editing\",\"categories\":[\"Media, journalism & propaganda\",\"Filmmaking & video production\"],\"tags\":[\"charlie brooker\",\"screenwipe\",\"editing\",\"reality tv\",\"media literacy\"],\"quote\":\"here is an awesome video that shows how editing can do wonders for how we perceive things(1).\",\"recommenders\":3,\"score\":2.5}",
    ",{\"vid\":\"BD6h-wDj7bw\",\"title\":\"Why Women Are Stripey\",\"channel\":\"Veritasium\",\"summary\":\"Veritasium explains X-chromosome inactivation, where different cells in a woman's body switch off different X chromosomes, giving a mosaic pattern. It uses animation from the WEHI institute and connects to calico cat coloring.\",\"why_hn\":\"Commenters point to it as the best short explanation of X inactivation and why calico cats and some human traits are mosaics.\",\"content_type\":\"explainer\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"x-chromosome inactivation\",\"categories\":[\"Evolution & genetics\",\"Biology & biotechnology\"],\"tags\":[\"epigenetics\",\"x-chromosome\",\"calico cats\",\"genetics\",\"mosaicism\"],\"quote\":\"Veritasium has a fantastic video that discusses the genetics behind the random color patterns of calico cats\",\"recommenders\":2,\"score\":2.5},{\"vid\":\"BHIo6qwJarI\",\"title\":\"Public Service Broadcasting - Go!\",\"channel\":\"PSBHQVEVO\",\"summary\":\"Music video for Public Service Broadcasting's \\\"Go!\\\" from the album The Race For Space, built from NASA audio and archival material of Apollo-era voices.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN recommends it as an energizing space-themed song, and references it when Apollo go/no-go calls come up.\",\"content_type\":\"music\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"space-themed music\",\"categories\":[\"Music performance & songs\",\"Space exploration & spaceflight\"],\"tags\":[\"public service broadcasting\",\"apollo\",\"race for space\",\"music video\",\"nasa samples\"],\"quote\":\"One of my favorite songs to listen to that can get a pumped up feeling\",\"recommenders\":2,\"score\":2.5},{\"vid\":\"BdHK_r9RXTc\",\"title\":\"Beats That Defy Boxes | Reggie Watts | TED\",\"channel\":\"TED\",\"summary\":\"Reggie Watts performs at TED 2012, blending vocal looping, beatboxing, poetry and comedy across musical genres in a larger-than-life improvised set.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN points to it as a memorable performance that doubles as a parody of TED talks and a showcase of live vocal looping.\",\"content_type\":\"talk\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"vocal looping performance\",\"categories\":[\"Music performance & songs\",\"Stand-up & sketch comedy\"],\"tags\":[\"reggie watts\",\"ted talk\",\"beatboxing\",\"live looping\",\"comedy\"],\"quote\":\"His TED talk is one for the ages\",\"recommenders\":2,\"score\":2.5},{\"vid\":\"BnSUk0je6oo\",\"title\":\"John Carmack Facebook Connect 2021 Keynote\",\"channel\":\"UploadVR\",\"summary\":\"John Carmack's keynote at Facebook Connect 2021, where he speaks candidly about VR, Quest, and Meta's metaverse plans. He pushes back on hype and discusses retention and latency.\",\"why_hn\":\"Commenters praise it as clear, honest thinking from Carmack and recommend it to technical people interested in VR and the metaverse.\",\"content_type\":\"talk\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"vr and the metaverse\",\"categories\":[\"VR, AR & spatial computing\",\"Tech pioneers & interviews\"],\"tags\":[\"john carmack\",\"meta quest\",\"metaverse\",\"virtual reality\",\"keynote\"],\"quote\":\"As always, John is a master of communication and clear thought.\",\"recommenders\":4,\"score\":2.5},{\"vid\":\"C7JQ7Rpwn2k\",\"title\":\"Sensor Fusion on Android Devices: A Revolution in Motion Processing\",\"channel\":\"Google TechTalks\",\"summary\":\"David Sachs of InvenSense explains how gyroscopes, accelerometers and compasses work on their own and together, demonstrated on a modified Android handset. He covers sensor fusion algorithms and why rotation math such as Euler angles matters.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN recommends it as the definitive talk on mobile motion sensing, including why integrating acceleration twice drifts so badly.\",\"content_type\":\"talk\",\"level\":\"advanced\",\"primary_topic\":\"sensor fusion\",\"categories\":[\"Embedded systems & DIY electronics\",\"Consumer devices & gadgets\"],\"tags\":[\"sensor fusion\",\"gyroscope\",\"accelerometer\",\"dead reckoning\",\"android\"],\"quote\":\"I'm always happy to share this incredible lecture from many many years ago\",\"recommenders\":2,\"score\":2.5},{\"vid\":\"CB-SCA1reqE\",\"title\":\"How to  Properly Heat a Pan\",\"channel\":\"Rouxbe\",\"summary\":\"A two-minute Rouxbe cooking-school demo of how to heat a pan properly before cooking. It uses the Leidenfrost effect, where water beads and skates across a hot pan, to show when a stainless steel pan is ready.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN people cite it as a practical test for pan temperature and as the way to get a stainless steel pan relatively non-stick.\",\"content_type\":\"tutorial\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"pan heating technique\",\"categories\":[\"Cooking & food\",\"Everyday physics & science demos\"],\"tags\":[\"cooking\",\"leidenfrost effect\",\"stainless steel pan\",\"pan frying\",\"kitchen technique\"],\"quote\":\"This youtube video explains the process\",\"recommenders\":2,\"score\":2.5},{\"vid\":\"Cfe5UQ-1L9Q\",\"title\":\"LIVE Coding \\\"Happy Jumping\\\"\",\"channel\":\"Inigo Quilez\",\"summary\":\"Inigo Quilez live-codes the \\\"Happy Jumping\\\" animated scene in a Shadertoy GLSL shader over about six hours. He builds the raymarched character step by step, explaining the math and procedural techniques, with checkpoints linked for each stage.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN commenters point to it as a patient, full-length walkthrough of how a raymarched shader is built from scratch.\",\"content_type\":\"tutorial\",\"level\":\"intermediate\",\"primary_topic\":\"raymarching shaders\",\"categories\":[\"Creative coding & generative art\",\"Computer graphics & rendering\"],\"tags\":[\"shadertoy\",\"glsl\",\"raymarching\",\"procedural animation\",\"live coding\",\"signed distance fields\"],\"quote\":\"is fantastic, yes it's five hours but worth it.\",\"recommenders\":2,\"score\":2.5},{\"vid\":\"D5in5EdjhD0\",\"title\":\"Noam Chomsky - \\\"The machine, the ghost, and the limits of understanding\\\"\",\"channel\":\"Andy80o\",\"summary\":\"Noam Chomsky's 2011 University of Oslo lecture on Newton's contributions to the study of mind. He argues Newton abandoned mechanical explanation and lowered the bar for scientific intelligibility, with consequences for the limits of human understanding. Q&A starts at 45:33.\",\"why_hn\":\"Recommended as a lucid, insightful lecture on the limits of human knowledge and the study of mind, one commenter calling it among the best lectures ever.\",\"content_type\":\"lecture\",\"level\":\"intermediate\",\"primary_topic\":\"philosophy of mind\",\"categories\":[\"Consciousness & cognition\",\"Philosophy & ethics\",\"Scientific method & science communication\"],\"tags\":[\"chomsky\",\"newton\",\"mind-body problem\",\"limits of knowledge\",\"history of science\"],\"quote\":\"Chomsky's surprisingly insightful thinking on the limits of human knowledge, and the consequences\",\"recommenders\":2,\"score\":2.5},{\"vid\":\"D7Kn5p7TP_Y\",\"title\":\"2017 Personality 18: Biology & Traits: Openness/Intelligence/Creativity I\",\"channel\":\"Jordan B Peterson\",\"summary\":\"A Jordan Peterson university lecture on the Big Five trait openness to experience, covering creativity and intelligence. It explains how IQ is measured, how well it predicts life success, and the Pareto distribution of creative output.\",\"why_hn\":\"Recommended as a solid introduction to personality and IQ research, and cited as the source for factor-analysis claims about personality and intelligence.\",\"content_type\":\"lecture\",\"level\":\"intro\",\"primary_topic\":\"personality psychology\",\"categories\":[\"Psychology & human behavior\",\"University lectures & courses\"],\"tags\":[\"big five\",\"openness\",\"iq\",\"creativity\",\"jordan peterson\"],\"quote\":\"For anybody interested in personality research, I warmly recommend this lecture series, by the way.\",\"recommenders\":2,\"score\":2.5},{\"vid\":\"DBxdTkddHaE\",\"title\":\"ARROWS vs ARMOUR - Medieval Myth Busting\",\"channel\":\"Tod's Workshop\",\"summary\":\"Tod's Workshop fires full-weight medieval arrows from a 160lb English warbow at reproduced medieval armour. Armour curator Dr Tobias Capwell, an archer and bowyer give historical context and discuss the results.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN considers it the key experimental evidence on how effective longbows really were against armour.\",\"content_type\":\"documentary\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"longbow versus plate armour\",\"categories\":[\"World history\",\"Military history & warfare\",\"Woodworking, metalworking & workshop skills\"],\"tags\":[\"longbow\",\"medieval armour\",\"experimental archaeology\",\"arrows\",\"history\"],\"quote\":\"I believe the video from Tod's Workshop with actual experimentation is a must see\",\"recommenders\":2,\"score\":2.5},{\"vid\":\"DQEB3LJ5psk\",\"title\":\"Always/Never: The Quest for Safety, Control, and Survivability - Part 1\",\"channel\":\"Sandia National Labs\",\"summary\":\"Part one of Sandia National Labs' first-person documentary on the use control, detonation safety and survivability of US nuclear weapons. It covers nuclear sharing in NATO and how control of use was separated from possession, leading to the always/never problem.\",\"why_hn\":\"Strongly recommended in nuclear-accident and weapons-history threads as an excellent documentary on how nuclear weapons were made safe and secure.\",\"content_type\":\"documentary\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"nuclear weapons safety\",\"categories\":[\"Military history & warfare\",\"Documentaries & storytelling\"],\"tags\":[\"sandia\",\"nuclear weapons\",\"use control\",\"cold war\",\"always/never\"],\"quote\":\"I highly recommend this three-part series produced by Sandia National Laboratory\",\"recommenders\":2,\"score\":2.5},{\"vid\":\"DXYje2B04xE\",\"title\":\"TSP #133 - Keysight UXR 110GHz BW, 256GS/s, 10-bit Real-Time Oscilloscope Teardown & Experiments\",\"channel\":\"The Signal Path\",\"summary\":\"Sha