etting in threads on greenwashing.\",\"content_type\":\"commentary\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"carbon offsets\",\"categories\":[\"Climate policy, solutions & debate\",\"Climate science & climate change\"],\"tags\":[\"carbon offsets\",\"greenwashing\",\"climate change\",\"climate town\",\"comedy\"],\"quote\":\"i'm taking the chance to share some content by people that present their points of view on this issue much better than i do\",\"recommenders\":2,\"score\":2.5},{\"vid\":\"ENLWEfi0Tkg\",\"title\":\"Gopherfest 2017 | Upspin with Rob Pike\",\"channel\":\"The Go Programming Language\",\"summary\":\"Rob Pike presents Upspin at Gopherfest 2017, an experimental framework for naming and sharing files and data securely and uniformly across a global namespace. It is a project written in Go rather than about Go.\",\"why_hn\":\"Cited as the talk that introduced Upspin, and called fascinating and really good by commenters.\",\"content_type\":\"talk\",\"level\":\"intermediate\",\"primary_topic\":\"upspin file sharing\",\"categories\":[\"C, C++, Rust, Go & systems languages\",\"Cryptography\",\"Tech pioneers & interviews\"],\"tags\":[\"upspin\",\"rob pike\",\"golang\",\"secure sharing\",\"naming systems\"],\"quote\":\"It's a fascinating talk. I really enjoyed it.\",\"recommenders\":2,\"score\":2.5},{\"vid\":\"EQs5VxNPhzk\",\"title\":\"[60 fps] The Flying Train, Germany, 1902\",\"channel\":\"Denis Shiryaev\",\"summary\":\"Neural-network upscaled, 60 fps, stabilized and colorized version of 1902 footage of the Wuppertal Schwebebahn suspended railway in Germany. The source film comes from MoMA. It gives a vivid view of an early-1900s city and a train system that still runs.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN commenters share it as a favorite example of upscaled vintage footage that makes the early 1900s feel present, though some find the colorization off.\",\"content_type\":\"demo\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"restored historical footage\",\"categories\":[\"World hi