unch.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN viewers were impressed by its speed and saw it as a glimpse of the future of voice search; later it appears in hiring posts.\",\"content_type\":\"demo\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"voice assistants\",\"categories\":[\"Computer vision, speech & NLP\",\"AI & data (other)\"],\"tags\":[\"hound\",\"soundhound\",\"voice search\",\"nlp\",\"siri\"],\"quote\":\"That's insanely fast, compound natural language queries. I'm impressed.\",\"recommenders\":2,\"score\":2.5},{\"vid\":\"MVYrJJNdrEg\",\"title\":\"Mark Zuckerberg: First Interview in the Metaverse | Lex Fridman Podcast #398\",\"channel\":\"Lex Fridman\",\"summary\":\"Lex Fridman interviews Mark Zuckerberg in the metaverse, with both appearing as photorealistic avatars from separate locations. They discuss Meta's AI, VR and the future of avatars.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN points to it as a demonstration that VR presence can feel close to talking in person.\",\"content_type\":\"podcast\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"virtual reality avatars\",\"categories\":[\"VR, AR & spatial computing\",\"Tech pioneers & interviews\"],\"tags\":[\"mark zuckerberg\",\"metaverse\",\"meta\",\"codec avatars\",\"lex fridman\"],\"quote\":\"The Fridman - Zuckerberg VR interview really convinced me of this, if you haven't seen it, check it out, it's incredible\",\"recommenders\":3,\"score\":2.5},{\"vid\":\"McLq1hEq3UY\",\"title\":\"Lecture 1 | Convex Optimization I (Stanford)\",\"channel\":\"Stanford\",\"summary\":\"The introductory lecture of Stephen Boyd's Stanford Convex Optimization I course (EE 364A). It outlines convex sets, functions and problems, and the course's coverage of least-squares, linear and semidefinite programming, duality and interior-point methods.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN recommends Boyd's lectures as a fantastic, often funny follow-up to linear algebra and as a step in machine learning study paths.\",\"content_type\":\"lecture\",\"level\":\"intermediate\",\"primary_topic\":\"convex optimization\",\"categories\":[\"University lectures & courses\",\"Pure mathematics\",\"Math & theory (other)\"],\"tags\":[\"convex optimization\",\"stanford\",\"linear algebra\",\"duality\",\"stephen boyd\"],\"quote\":\"These lectures are fantastic after you've mastered the basics of linear algebra\",\"recommenders\":2,\"score\":2.5},{\"vid\":\"MnrJzXM7a6o\",\"title\":\"Steve Jobs introduces iPhone in 2007\",\"channel\":\"John Schroter\",\"summary\":\"An excerpt from Steve Jobs's January 2007 Macworld keynote in which he introduces the original iPhone. It shows the pitch of a phone, music player and internet communicator, along with the live demo.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN treats it as the model product demo and MVP showcase, and as a reminder of how constrained the first iPhone hardware was.\",\"content_type\":\"demo\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"iphone launch keynote\",\"categories\":[\"Tech pioneers & interviews\",\"Consumer devices & gadgets\",\"Tech company stories & documentaries\"],\"tags\":[\"steve jobs\",\"iphone\",\"keynote\",\"product demo\",\"apple\",\"mvp\"],\"quote\":\"If you want to se the ultimate MVP demo of a product look no further than the 2007 introduction of the Apple iPhone\",\"recommenders\":3,\"score\":2.5}",
