ramming and GUIs. He discusses how poorly people understand complex systems and what education could do about it.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN readers cite Kay's talks for his views on programming languages as user interfaces, thinking beyond logic, and why people struggle with complex systems.\",\"content_type\":\"talk\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"computer science education\",\"categories\":[\"Education & learning\",\"Tech pioneers & interviews\",\"Software architecture & design\"],\"tags\":[\"alan kay\",\"education\",\"systems thinking\",\"programming languages\",\"learning\"],\"quote\":\"I would really really encourage everyone here to watch Alan Kay's recent talks on how poorly we understand systems\",\"recommenders\":2,\"score\":2.5},{\"vid\":\"ND2TeNfcmKA\",\"title\":\"Toxic Propellant Hazards In Rocketry 1966 NASA\",\"channel\":\"markdcatlin\",\"summary\":\"A 1966 NASA safety film teaching workers how to handle toxic rocket propellants such as hydrazine and nitrogen tetroxide. It explains the hazards of these corrosive, flammable and toxic chemicals and what to do after contamination.\",\"why_hn\":\"Commenters share it as a favorite vintage NASA film with a sobering look at how dangerous hypergolic propellants are.\",\"content_type\":\"documentary\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"rocket propellant safety\",\"categories\":[\"Space exploration & spaceflight\",\"Chemistry\"],\"tags\":[\"nasa\",\"hydrazine\",\"nitrogen tetroxide\",\"hypergolic\",\"safety film\",\"rocketry\"],\"quote\":\"provides an interesting discussion of the dangers of nitrogen tetroxide and hydrazine propellants.\",\"recommenders\":2,\"score\":2.5},{\"vid\":\"NIu_dJGyIQI\",\"title\":\"Free Energy Principle — Karl Friston\",\"channel\":\"Serious Science\",\"summary\":\"Neuroscientist Karl Friston gives a 15-minute talk on the free energy principle, covering Markov blankets, Bayesian model evidence and global brain theories.\",\"why_hn\":\"Offered as a high-level, approachable in