ty builder\",\"kowloon walled city\",\"games\"],\"quote\":\"Don't miss the video\",\"recommenders\":2,\"score\":2.5},{\"vid\":\"NmGaXEmfTIo\",\"title\":\"The Computer-free Automation of a Jukebox (Electromechanics)\",\"channel\":\"Technology Connections\",\"summary\":\"Technology Connections takes apart a 1970 Wurlitzer 3400 jukebox to show how electromechanical relays and switches automated its behavior without a computer.\",\"why_hn\":\"Recommended as an eye-opening look at pre-computer automation and relay logic.\",\"content_type\":\"explainer\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"electromechanical automation\",\"categories\":[\"Mechanical & precision engineering\",\"Electronics & circuit design\",\"History of computing\"],\"tags\":[\"jukebox\",\"relays\",\"electromechanics\",\"wurlitzer\",\"vintage technology\"],\"quote\":\"The computer free automation of a jukebox from the 1970s is an eye opener\",\"recommenders\":2,\"score\":2.5},{\"vid\":\"Nsjsiz2A9mg\",\"title\":\"Robert C Martin - Clean Architecture and Design\",\"channel\":\"gnbitcom\",\"summary\":\"Robert C. Martin (Uncle Bob) talks about clean architecture and design, including keeping the database and frameworks out of the center of an application. It is an hour-long conference talk.\",\"why_hn\":\"Recommended as a formative talk on architecture that argues against putting the database at the center of a design.\",\"content_type\":\"talk\",\"level\":\"intermediate\",\"primary_topic\":\"software architecture\",\"categories\":[\"Software architecture & design\"],\"tags\":[\"clean architecture\",\"uncle bob\",\"software design\",\"layering\",\"dependencies\"],\"quote\":\"This talk was really formative for me\",\"recommenders\":2,\"score\":2.5},{\"vid\":\"ODSJsviD_SU\",\"title\":\"Tesla AI Day 2022\",\"channel\":\"Tesla\",\"summary\":\"Tesla's full AI Day 2022 presentation, covering the Tesla Bot hardware and software, Full Self-Driving planning and perception, the occupancy network, data labeling, simulation and Dojo training infrastructure.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN uses it as primary-source evidence on how Tesla's vision-based driving stack and training pipeline work.\",\"content_type\":\"talk\",\"level\":\"advanced\",\"primary_topic\":\"self-driving AI\",\"categories\":[\"Self-driving & autonomous vehicles\",\"Robotics\",\"Machine learning & deep learning\"],\"tags\":[\"tesla\",\"full self-driving\",\"occupancy networks\",\"dojo\",\"humanoid robots\",\"computer vision\"],\"quote\":\"Learning about their engineering in that regard really changed my perception of the likelihood that they could solve the problem. Give it a watch\",\"recommenders\":2,\"score\":2.5},{\"vid\":\"OL6-x0modwY\",\"title\":\"The Scientific Method-Richard Feynman\",\"channel\":\"Sképseis\",\"summary\":\"A one-minute clip of Richard Feynman describing the scientific method: guess a law, compute its consequences, and compare with experiment. If it disagrees with experiment, it is wrong.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN quotes it as the crispest statement of what science is, usually when a theory clashes with evidence.\",\"content_type\":\"lecture\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"scientific method\",\"categories\":[\"Scientific method & science communication\",\"Fundamental physics\"],\"tags\":[\"feynman\",\"scientific method\",\"experiment\",\"philosophy of science\"],\"quote\":\"That is the scientific method. And it is presented by one of our best ever thinkers.\",\"recommenders\":2,\"score\":2.5},{\"vid\":\"Ocq3NeudsVk\",\"title\":\"Sonification & The Problem with Making Music from Data\",\"channel\":\"Tantacrul\",\"summary\":\"Tantacrul examines sonification, the practice of turning data into sound or music, and critiques how scientists and musicians, including NASA and CERN projects, use it well and poorly.\",\"why_hn\":\"Recommended as an incisive look at the real potential and common misuse of data sonification, often brought up in threads on space sonifications.\",\"content_type\":\"commentary\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"data sonification\",\"categories\":[\"Music theory, synthesis & production\",\"Data visualization & information design\"],\"tags\":[\"sonification\",\"music\",\"data\",\"nasa\",\"audification\"],\"quote\":\"Tantacrul has a typically incisive video [1] about the real potential of sonification as a powerful technique for understanding data\",\"recommenders\":2,\"score\":2.5},{\"vid\":\"Og6cTlwBTrk\",\"title\":\"Building the Moroccan Court\",\"channel\":\"The Met\",\"summary\":\"A short film following Moroccan artisans from Fez as they build a traditional 15th-century-style Moroccan court inside the Metropolitan Museum of Art. It shows zellij tilework and other traditional techniques.\",\"why_hn\":\"Shared as a satisfying look at craftsmen taking pride in traditional handmade tile mosaics.\",\"content_type\":\"documentary\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"traditional moroccan craftsmanship\",\"categories\":[\"Visual arts, photography & architecture\",\"Woodworking, metalworking & workshop skills\",\"Civil engineering & construction\"],\"tags\":[\"zellij\",\"tilework\",\"morocco\",\"craftsmanship\",\"islamic art\"],\"quote\":\"Here’s a great video [0][17min] documenting the Met Museum’s commissioning of moroccan mosaics\",\"recommenders\":2,\"score\":2.5},{\"vid\":\"Oie1ZXWceqM\",\"title\":\"3-Sweep: Extracting Editable Objects from a Single Photo, SIGGRAPH ASIA 2013\",\"channel\":\"Daniel CohenOr\",\"summary\":\"A SIGGRAPH Asia 2013 research demo of 3-Sweep, a tool for extracting editable 3D objects from a single photo using a few user strokes. It predates modern AI image tools.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN recalls it as a mind-blowing pre-AI demo of 2D-to-3D object extraction.\",\"content_type\":\"demo\",\"level\":\"intermediate\",\"primary_topic\":\"single-image 3d reconstruction\",\"categories\":[\"Computer vision, speech & NLP\",\"Computer graphics & rendering\"],\"tags\":[\"3d modeling\",\"siggraph\",\"computer vision\",