":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"stand-up comedy\",\"categories\":[\"Stand-up & sketch comedy\"],\"tags\":[\"paul taylor\",\"franglais\",\"france\",\"expat life\",\"british humour\"],\"quote\":\"I HIGHLY recommend a watch, it's hilarious especially if you're familiar with both French and British/American culture\",\"recommenders\":2,\"score\":2.5},{\"vid\":\"PaypcVFPs48\",\"title\":\"Building Prototypes Dan Gelbart  part 10 of 18  Flexures\",\"channel\":\"Dan Gelbart\",\"summary\":\"Part 10 of Dan Gelbart's prototype-building lecture series, covering flexures: flexible joints that give precise, frictionless motion. It shows how a cheap piece of aluminum can become a nanometer-accurate mechanism.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN recommends the series as a fascinating, practical course in precision prototyping, with the flexure episode singled out as especially impressive.\",\"content_type\":\"lecture\",\"level\":\"intermediate\",\"primary_topic\":\"flexure mechanisms\",\"categories\":[\"Mechanical & precision engineering\",\"3D printing, CNC & maker projects\"],\"tags\":[\"flexures\",\"precision engineering\",\"prototyping\",\"mechanical design\",\"machining\"],\"quote\":\"He starts off with a \$10 piece of aluminum that took maybe an hour or two to make\",\"recommenders\":2,\"score\":2.5},{\"vid\":\"PlJkgQZb0VU\",\"title\":\"Brian Springer - Spin\",\"channel\":\"MasterpieceConCen7\",\"summary\":\"Brian Springer's documentary Spin, built entirely from unauthorized satellite feeds of politicians and newscasters before they went on air during the 1992 US presidential election. It exposes the behind-the-scenes construction of media reality.\",\"why_hn\":\"Recommended as a revealing look at how politicians and news anchors behave off camera and how packaged news feeds were produced.\",\"content_type\":\"documentary\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"media and politics\",\"categories\":[\"Media, journalism & propaganda\",\"US politics & elections\",\"Documentaries & storytelling\"],\"tags\":[\"spin\",\"brian springer\",\"1992 election\",\"satellite feeds\",\"news media\"],\"quote\":\"You might like Spin , a 1995 documentary composed of unauthorized behind the scenes footage\",\"recommenders\":2,\"score\":2.5},{\"vid\":\"PsXFwy6gG_4\",\"title\":\"Eric Schmidt and Peter Thiel - Fortune Debate, 2012\",\"channel\":\"kykeon\",\"summary\":\"A 2012 Fortune dinner debate between Peter Thiel and Eric Schmidt over whether technological progress is healthy or stalling and whether Google can still innovate.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN recalls it as one of the most interesting debates between two contrasting worldviews on progress.\",\"content_type\":\"talk\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"technological progress\",\"categories\":[\"Futurism & technology and society\",\"Tech industry & business models\",\"Tech pioneers & interviews\"],\"tags\":[\"peter thiel\",\"eric schmidt\",\"innovation\",\"debate\",\"google\"],\"quote\":\"One of the most interesting debates was between Eric Schmidt and Peter Thiel back in 2012\",\"recommenders\":2,\"score\":2.5},{\"vid\":\"PsgBtOVzHKI\",\"title\":\"Feynman: Take the world from another point of view (1/4)\",\"channel\":\"Aaron Scher\",\"summary\":\"Part one of a four-part upload of a BBC Horizon documentary featuring Richard Feynman, in which he talks about physics and looking at the world from another point of view.\",\"why_hn\":\"Mentioned as a fun and impressive Feynman documentary, though the mentions are brief.\",\"content_type\":\"documentary\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"richard feynman\",\"categories\":[\"Fundamental physics\",\"Scientific method & science communication\",\"Documentaries & storytelling\"],\"tags\":[\"richard feynman\",\"physics\",\"horizon\",\"documentary\",\"scientific thinking\"],\"quote\":\"I love this old Horizon as well\",\"recommenders\":2,\"score\":2.5},{\"vid\":\"Q0yL2GezneU\",\"title\":\"Vocal Fry: what it is, who does it, and why people hate it!\",\"channel\":\"Dr Geoff Lindsey\",\"summary\":\"Linguist Geoff Lindsey explores vocal fry: what it is, who uses it, how it relates to glottal stops and accents, and why some people dislike it.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN points to it as an expert correction of myths about vocal fry, showing it is a normal speech pattern across groups.\",\"content_type\":\"explainer\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"vocal fry\",\"categories\":[\"Language & linguistics\"],\"tags\":[\"vocal fry\",\"phonetics\",\"linguistics\",\"gender and speech\",\"accents\"],\"quote\":\"it's not just that. It's (also?) a normal speech pattern, used by different genders, ages, and social groups, in many languages.\",\"recommenders\":2,\"score\":2.5},{\"vid\":\"QAr-uHd8h8o\",\"title\":\"Why Figure 8 knot is NOT hard to untie!\",\"channel\":\"Hard Is Easy\",\"summary\":\"Hard Is Easy runs experiments to show that a correctly tied figure 8 knot is not hard to untie after loading. He shows how two knots that look similar can behave differently depending on how they are dressed.\",\"why_hn\":\"Cited in climbing knot threads to counter the claim that figure 8s jam, by showing the correct tying method.\",\"content_type\":\"demo\",\"level\":\"intro\",\"primary_topic\":\"climbing knots\",\"categories\":[\"Sports & athletics\",\"Everyday physics & science demos\"],\"tags\":[\"figure 8 knot\",\"rock climbing\",\"knot experiments\",\"climbing safety\",\"bowline\"],\"quote\":\"Apparently there is a wrong way of tying a figure 8, that leads to a version that is much harder to untie.\",\"recommenders\":2,\"score\":2.5},{\"vid\":\"QCAL_YgYiP0\",\"title\":\"DEF CON 18 - Jason Scott - You're Stealing It Wrong! 30 Years of Inter-Pirate Battles\",\"channel\":\"DEFCONConference\",\"summary\":\"Jason Scott's DEF CON 18 talk tells the history of software piracy over thirty years, centered on the feuds and drama among rival warez groups. It is full of archival material and insider lingo.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN brings it up in threads on warez, cracktros and the demoscene as a funny, informative history of the piracy scene.\",\"content_type\":\"talk\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"software piracy history\",\"categories\":[\"Hacker culture & free software\",\"History of computing\",\"Demoscene & retrocomputing\"],\"tags\":[\"warez\",\"jason scott\",\"def con\",\"demoscene\",\"computer history\"],\"quote\":\"Related, and a personal favorite of mine\",\"recommenders\":2,\"score\":2.5},{\"vid\":\"QHPmRJIoc2k\",\"title\":\"Tom Lehrer Full Copenhagen Performance\",\"channel\":\"Tom Lehrer\",\"summary\":\"A full-length recording of Tom Lehrer's 1967 concert in Copenhagen, mixing his satirical songs with spoken comedy between numbers. It runs about 51 minutes with good audio for its age.\",\"why_hn\":\"Posted whenever Lehrer comes up, as the best way to see him perform, and treated as a complete stand-up-style set.\",\"content_type\":\"music\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"tom lehrer concert\",\"categories\":[\"Music performance & songs\",\"Stand-up & sketch comedy\",\"Satire & parody\"],\"tags\":[\"tom lehrer\",\"satirical songs\",\"live concert\",\"comedy\",\"1960s\"],\"quote\":\"He intersperses song and spoken comedy, with the whole performance hanging together masterfully.\",\"recommenders\":2,\"score\":2.5},{\"vid\":\"QHnLmvDxGTY\",\"title\":\"\\\"Uncle\\\" Bob Martin\",\"channel\":\"Program on Entrepreneurship\",\"summary\":\"Robert 'Uncle Bob' Martin speaks at Yale School of Management about clean, well-written code and what makes good software development. The talk covers his views on OOP, architecture and professional practice.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN cites it as a formative talk on what OOP really is, and on why teams write code that slows them down.\",\"content_type\":\"talk\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"clean code and oop\",\"categories\":[\"Software architecture & design\",\"Software practice, open source & careers\"],\"tags\":[\"uncle bob\",\"clean code\",\"oop\",\"softwar